      "The conductor is a thin executor of typed supervisor actions, not a lifecycle judge. Before every actor dispatch, phase transition, review retry, story close, or epic close, run exactly one `.acef/bin/acef-supervisor --repo .` call and perform only its typed action. If the action is blocked/replan or disagrees with repository state, stop fail-closed instead of interpreting the workflow in prose.",
      "When the supervisor returns prepare-review-capsules, run its exact model-free scopeCommand. On cycle 0, commit the control-only review transition only when review-scope reports WROTE; on retry cycles revalidate only and do not create an early repair-layer commit. Then generate exactly the role capsules listed by the action from the resulting shared HEAD. This re-derives surfaces from the committed production delta and frozen worker scope without inventing bootstrap labels or placeholder Judge artifacts.",
      "Create the supervisor-listed role-specific hash-bound review capsules before dispatching reviewers. A reviewer begins with exactly one capsule-show call, consumes the bound focused-runner proof, may make a targeted hash-bound read only for a named uncertainty, then emits exactly one review-result command. Do not rerun the focused command unless a named evidence conflict requires adjudication. The capsules share raw evidence but never another reviewer's conclusion; after a test-only repair, a prior Code Review PASS may be retained while Patch Assurance alone reruns.",
