      "The original Developer remains one session for the story. It may perform bounded focused-test attempts inside its original turn and one repair follow-up per review cycle, but it must not return on the first failed attempt. It returns only with accepted discovered green evidence and, for a repair, one final repair receipt; a terminal non-green return is REPLAN/SPLIT, never another continuation or replacement Developer.",
      "Mechanical state transitions, evidence collection, capsule generation, report generation, and gate construction use deterministic tools. Do not delegate them or ask a model to restate their JSON. The manifest-pinned Sol/high semantic actors remain unchanged in this first candidate; the Terra/medium thin-proxy profile is shadow-only and cannot certify the run.",
    ].join("\n")
    : "";
  return [
    "Complete one controlled multi-story epic in this disposable clone. The measured unit is the complete original user outcome, not an individual story.",
    treatmentInstruction,
    fourActorV3
      ? "This prompt is the complete compiled ACEF contract for the scored run. Do not reread ACEF/BMAD method documents or ask child actors to load linked workflow files; the installed skill entry may be consulted only when host policy requires it, without following links outside the active artifact allowlist. Run readiness and reuse checks as deterministic conductor gates, not extra persona workers. The actor rows listed below are the exhaustive base lifecycle inventory. Preserve actor separation; do not self-approve."
      : "Load and follow the repo-local ACEF skill. Act as conductor and use fresh independent actors/sessions for every role the installed workflow requires. Preserve actor separation; do not self-approve.",
    "For each contract row below, call spawn_agent exactly once using the exact task_name, fork_turns=none, model, and reasoning_effort printed on that row before accepting that phase. Model/effort routing is imposed by the manifest; no actor may select or downgrade its own runtime. Give the fresh actor a bounded artifact-only message: put the listed scope/control/actor/persona tuple first, then only the exact files/commit/question it needs. Do not ask the actor to reread ACEF/BMAD workflow documents. Limit its initial read envelope to the current context plus at most six exact task files and 300 lines per read; targeted follow-up reads are allowed only when a named unresolved question requires them. If it cannot identify progress within ten active minutes, it must return ACTOR_RESULT=REVISE with the exact bottleneck instead of broadening inspection. Accept `ACTOR_RESULT=PASS` and the semantically identical `ACTOR_RESULT: PASS` spelling; likewise for REVISE. Wait for that actor's FINAL_ANSWER and persist a typed actor record whose actorInstanceId exactly equals task_name, except that v3 ATDD evidence-run and each v3 reviewer completion atomically own their respective actor records. For Development, set actor sessionId to the exact canonical /root/<task_name> identity returned by spawn_agent, never to the bare task_name or an unobservable internal receiver UUID; the harness independently binds that path to the child session UUID. Do not combine rows in one actor. For ATDD, commit the clean test-only red tree before invoking evidence-run; never bind red evidence while a production or test path is dirty.",
    recoveryInstruction,
    runtimeInstruction,
    fourActorV3
      ? `ATDD and development are single mandatory actor identities. Code Review and Patch Assurance may each use at most two fresh, affected-only delta retry actors after a developer repair; the ${manifest.promotionGates.budget.maximumActorInvocations}-invocation epic cap still binds. Story Process Judge is optional only for the four named triggers. The epic Process Judge cannot retry. Never replay a complete lifecycle.`
      : attempt.treatment === "candidate"
      ? "Development and test-review cannot be retried. Code-review, verify-patch, and story process-judge may each use at most one retry only after ACTOR_RESULT=REVISE; its exact task_name must be <base>_retry1 and it must finish ACTOR_RESULT=PASS. The epic Process Judge cannot retry. Never replay a full lifecycle vector."
      : "The exact named rows below remain the minimum independently observable lifecycle contract; legacy-required auxiliary work remains allowed and measured.",
    fourActorV3
      ? "Each story must have a deterministic typed PASS gate computed from its four actor records and final-tree evidence. After the one final integration verification, the separate epic Process Judge must persist a typed PASS gate with scope=epic and must not be any story actor."
      : "Each story Process Judge must persist a typed PASS gate for that story. After the one final integration verification, the separate epic Process Judge must persist a typed PASS gate with scope=epic and must not be any story actor.",
    "Required independently observable actor contract:",
    actorContract,
    "If readiness requires splitting or replanning, record and perform it, but the outcome clock continues until the complete epic is product-done.",
    closeoutInstruction,
    "Before every write, reconcile the exact target against the active story's allowed paths and protected paths. A worker must refuse the write before mutation when it is outside scope; post-hoc cleanup does not cure a scope violation.",
    "Do not inspect experiment manifests, sibling worktrees, previous transcripts, or the other treatment. Do not push. Do not weaken or edit Benchmark* tests or phpunit.sqlite.xml.",
    "Frozen epic stories:",
    stories,
    `Final integration verification: ${resolved.task.integration.verify.join(" ")}`,
    "Final response must state RESULT=PASS or RESULT=FAIL, product outcome, story results, review rounds, broad-suite runs, unresolved Critical/High risks, and exact closeout status.",
  ].join("\n");
}

function sha256File(filePath) {
  return crypto.createHash("sha256").update(fs.readFileSync(filePath)).digest("hex");
}

function normalizedActorToken(value) {
  return String(value || "").toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "_").replace(/^_+|_+$/g, "");
}

function lifecycleActorContract(resolved, version = "six-actor-v2") {
  const phases = version === "four-actor-v3" ? [
    ["atdd", "test-author", false],
    ["development", "developer", false],
    ["code-review", "code-reviewer", true],
    ["patch-assurance", "patch-assurance-reviewer", true],
  ] : [
    ["atdd", "test-author", false],
    ["development", "developer", false],
    ["code-review", "code-reviewer", true],
    ["verify-patch", "patch-verifier", true],
    ["test-review", "test-reviewer", false],
    ["process-judge", "process-judge", true],
  ];
  const storyEntries = resolved.task.stories.flatMap((story) => phases.map(([control, persona, retryable]) => ({
    scope: story.id,
    control,
    persona,
    retryable,
    taskName: `acef_${normalizedActorToken(story.id)}_${normalizedActorToken(control)}`,
  })));
  return [...storyEntries, {
    scope: "epic",
    control: "process-judge",
    persona: "process-judge",
    retryable: false,
    taskName: "acef_epic_process_judge",
  }];
}

function findCodexSessionTranscript(threadId, sessionRoot = path.join(process.env.CODEX_HOME || path.join(os.homedir(), ".codex"), "sessions")) {
  if (!threadId || !fs.existsSync(sessionRoot)) return null;
  const pending = [sessionRoot];
  while (pending.length) {
    const directory = pending.pop();
    for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(directory, { withFileTypes: true })) {
      const fullPath = path.join(directory, entry.name);
      if (entry.isDirectory()) pending.push(fullPath);
      else if (entry.isFile() && entry.name.includes(threadId) && entry.name.endsWith(".jsonl")) return fullPath;
    }
  }
  return null;
}

function actorResultFromText(value) {
  return String(value || "").match(/\bACTOR_RESULT\s*(?:=|:)\s*(PASS|REVISE|FAIL|BLOCKED|REPLAN)\b/i)?.[1]?.toUpperCase() || "";
}

function actorResultIs(value, expected) {
  return actorResultFromText(value) === expected;
}

function conditionalJudgeTrigger(parentFinalText, cwd, taskName) {
  let trigger = String(parentFinalText || "")
    .match(/\bJUDGE_TRIGGER=(AMBIGUITY|WAIVER|EVIDENCE[_-]CONFLICT|GATE[_-]ANOMALY)\b/i)?.[1] || "";
  if (!trigger && cwd) {
    try {
      const parser = installedStateParser(cwd);
      const actor = parser.parseActorRecord(path.join(cwd, "docs", "ai", "actors", `${taskName}.json`));
      const decision = parser.parseProcessJudgeDecision(path.resolve(cwd, actor.producedArtifactPath));
      trigger = decision.trigger || "";
    } catch {}
  }
  const normalized = String(trigger).toLowerCase().replace(/_/g, "-");
  return ["ambiguity", "waiver", "evidence-conflict", "gate-anomaly"].includes(normalized) ? normalized : "";
}

function developerActorSessionBound(cwd, taskName, canonicalAgentPath) {
  if (!cwd || !taskName || !canonicalAgentPath) return false;
  try {
    const actor = installedStateParser(cwd)
      .parseActorRecord(path.join(cwd, "docs", "ai", "actors", `${taskName}.json`));
    return actor.actorInstanceId === taskName && canonicalAgentPath === `/root/${taskName}`
      && actor.sessionId === canonicalAgentPath;
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}

function reviewerResultFromReport(repoRoot, taskName) {
  if (!repoRoot || !taskName) return "";
  try {
    const report = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(repoRoot, "docs", "ai", "reports", `${taskName}.json`), "utf8"));
    if (report.schema !== "acef.review-report.v3" || report.actorInstanceId !== taskName) return "";
    return ["PASS", "REVISE"].includes(report.verdict) ? report.verdict : "";
  } catch {
    return "";
  }
}

function parseCollaborationEvidence(rawText, sessionText, expectedContract, expectedSession = {}) {
  let threadId = null;
  for (const line of String(rawText || "").split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)) {
    try {
      const event = JSON.parse(line);
      if (event.type === "thread.started") threadId = event.thread_id || null;
    } catch {}
  }
  const calls = new Map();
  const followups = [];
  const started = new Map();
  const terminalInfrastructureFailures = new Map();
  const completedAuthors = new Map();
  let sessionMeta = null;
  for (const line of String(sessionText || "").split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)) {
    let event;
    try { event = JSON.parse(line); } catch { continue; }
    const payload = event.payload || {};
    if (event.type === "session_meta") sessionMeta = payload;
    if (event.type === "response_item" && payload.type === "function_call"
      && payload.namespace === "collaboration" && payload.name === "spawn_agent") {
      let args = {};
      try { args = JSON.parse(payload.arguments || "{}"); } catch {}
      calls.set(payload.call_id, {
        taskName: args.task_name || "",
        forkTurns: args.fork_turns,
        model: args.model || null,
        reasoningEffort: args.reasoning_effort || null,
        message: args.message || "",
        callId: payload.call_id,
        spawnedAt: event.timestamp || null,
      });
    }
    if (event.type === "response_item" && payload.type === "function_call"
      && payload.namespace === "collaboration" && payload.name === "followup_task") {
      let args = {};
      try { args = JSON.parse(payload.arguments || "{}"); } catch {}
      followups.push({
        target: args.target || "",
        callId: payload.call_id,
        calledAt: event.timestamp || null,
      });
    }
    if (event.type === "event_msg" && payload.type === "sub_agent_activity" && payload.kind === "started") {
      started.set(payload.event_id, payload.agent_thread_id || "");
    }
    if (event.type === "event_msg" && payload.type === "sub_agent_activity"
      && payload.kind === "failed" && payload.infrastructureFailure) {
      terminalInfrastructureFailures.set(payload.event_id, {
        eventTimestamp: event.timestamp || null,
        receiverThreadId: payload.agent_thread_id || "",
        receipt: payload.infrastructureFailure,
      });
    }
    if (event.type === "response_item" && payload.type === "agent_message" && payload.author) {
      const content = Array.isArray(payload.content)
        ? payload.content.map((entry) => entry.text || entry.output_text || "").join("\n")
        : String(payload.text || "");
      const list = completedAuthors.get(payload.author) || [];
      list.push({ content, deliveredAt: event.timestamp || null });
      completedAuthors.set(payload.author, list);
    }
  }
  const dispatches = [...calls.values()].map((call) => {
    const delivered = [...(completedAuthors.get(`/root/${call.taskName}`) || []), ...(completedAuthors.get(call.taskName) || [])]
      .find((entry) => /Message Type:\s*FINAL_ANSWER/i.test(entry.content)
        && new RegExp(`Sender:\\s*\\/root\\/${call.taskName}(?:\\s|$)`).test(entry.content));
    return {
      ...call,
      receiverThreadId: started.get(call.callId) || "",
      parentFinalText: delivered?.content || "",
      finalDeliveredAt: delivered?.deliveredAt || null,
    };
  });
  const failures = [];
  if (!sessionMeta) failures.push("session metadata missing");
  else {
    if (sessionMeta.session_id !== threadId) failures.push("session id does not match stdout thread.started");
    if (expectedSession.cwd && fs.realpathSync(sessionMeta.cwd) !== fs.realpathSync(expectedSession.cwd)) failures.push("session cwd mismatch");
    if (expectedSession.clientVersion && sessionMeta.cli_version !== expectedSession.clientVersion) failures.push("session client version mismatch");
    if (expectedSession.startedAt && new Date(sessionMeta.timestamp) < new Date(new Date(expectedSession.startedAt).getTime() - 60000)) failures.push("session predates actor receipt");
    if (expectedSession.finishedAt && new Date(sessionMeta.timestamp) > new Date(new Date(expectedSession.finishedAt).getTime() + 60000)) failures.push("session postdates actor receipt");
  }
  const relevant = [];
  const acceptedActors = [];
  const observedContract = [];
  const correctionBindings = [];
  const knownTaskNames = new Set();
  const infrastructureFailureReceipts = [];
  const boundFollowupCallIds = new Set();
  const legacyPolicy = expectedSession.legacyPolicy === true;
  const fourActorV3 = expectedSession.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3";
  const dispatchResult = (entry, control = "") => fourActorV3 && expectedSession.cwd
    && ["code-review", "patch-assurance"].includes(control)
    ? reviewerResultFromReport(expectedSession.cwd, entry.taskName)
    : actorResultFromText(entry.parentFinalText);
  const maximumRetryOrdinal = fourActorV3 ? 2 : 1;
  const selectPhysicalInvocation = (logicalTaskName) => {
    const originals = dispatches.filter((entry) => entry.taskName === logicalTaskName);
    if (!fourActorV3) return originals;
    const infrastructure = dispatches.map((entry) => {
      const match = entry.taskName.match(new RegExp(`^${logicalTaskName}_infra_retry([1-9]\\d*)$`));
      return match ? { ...entry, infrastructureRetryOrdinal: Number(match[1]), logicalTaskName } : null;
    }).filter(Boolean);
    knownTaskNames.add(logicalTaskName);
    for (const entry of infrastructure) knownTaskNames.add(entry.taskName);
    if (originals.length !== 1) failures.push(`${logicalTaskName}: expected one original invocation, observed ${originals.length}`);
    if (infrastructure.length > 1 || infrastructure.some((entry) => entry.infrastructureRetryOrdinal !== 1)) {
      failures.push(`${logicalTaskName}: infrastructure retry allows only _infra_retry1`);
    }
    if (infrastructure.length && originals.some((entry) => entry.parentFinalText)) {
      failures.push(`${logicalTaskName}: infrastructure retry requires original invocation without FINAL_ANSWER`);
    }
    if (infrastructure.length && originals.length === 1) {
      const original = originals[0];
      const retry = infrastructure[0];
      const terminal = terminalInfrastructureFailures.get(original.callId);
      const receipt = terminal?.receipt;
      const originalStartedAt = Date.parse(original.spawnedAt || "");
      const failureStartedAt = Date.parse(receipt?.startedAt || "");
      const failureFinishedAt = Date.parse(receipt?.finishedAt || "");
      const failureEventAt = Date.parse(terminal?.eventTimestamp || "");
      const retryStartedAt = Date.parse(retry.spawnedAt || "");
      const validReceipt = receipt?.schema === "acef.infrastructure-failure.v1"
        && receipt.terminal === true && receipt.taskName === logicalTaskName
        && receipt.receiverThreadId === original.receiverThreadId
        && terminal?.receiverThreadId === original.receiverThreadId
        && /^[a-f0-9]{40,64}$/.test(receipt.preTree || "") && receipt.postTree === receipt.preTree
        && Array.isArray(receipt.writePaths) && receipt.writePaths.length === 0
        && typeof receipt.reasonCode === "string" && receipt.reasonCode.length > 0
        && [originalStartedAt, failureStartedAt, failureFinishedAt, failureEventAt, retryStartedAt].every(Number.isFinite)
        && failureStartedAt >= originalStartedAt && failureFinishedAt >= failureStartedAt
        && failureEventAt >= failureFinishedAt && retryStartedAt > failureEventAt;
      if (!validReceipt) {
        failures.push(`${logicalTaskName}: infrastructure retry requires a typed terminal failure receipt, zero-write tree, and non-overlapping retry ordering`);
      } else {
        infrastructureFailureReceipts.push({
          logicalTaskName, originalTaskName: original.taskName, retryTaskName: retry.taskName,
          originalCallId: original.callId, retryCallId: retry.callId, ...receipt,
        });
      }
    }
    return infrastructure.length ? infrastructure.slice(0, 1) : originals;
  };
  for (const expected of expectedContract) {
    const baseMatches = selectPhysicalInvocation(expected.taskName);
    const retryLogicalNames = [...new Set(dispatches.map((entry) => entry.taskName.replace(/_infra_retry[1-9]\d*$/, ""))
      .filter((taskName) => new RegExp(`^${expected.taskName}_retry[1-9]\\d*$`).test(taskName)))];
    const retryMatches = retryLogicalNames.flatMap((logicalTaskName) => {
      const retryOrdinal = Number(logicalTaskName.match(/_retry([1-9]\d*)$/)?.[1] || 0);
      return selectPhysicalInvocation(logicalTaskName).map((entry) => ({ ...entry, retryOrdinal, logicalTaskName }));
    }).sort((left, right) => left.retryOrdinal - right.retryOrdinal);
    knownTaskNames.add(expected.taskName);
    for (const retry of retryMatches) knownTaskNames.add(retry.taskName);
    if (baseMatches.length !== 1 && !fourActorV3) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: expected one base spawn, observed ${baseMatches.length}`);
    if (!legacyPolicy && retryMatches.length && !expected.retryable) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: retries are not allowed for ${expected.control}`);
    if (!legacyPolicy && retryMatches.length > maximumRetryOrdinal) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: circuit breaker allows at most ${maximumRetryOrdinal} retries`);
    if (!legacyPolicy && !fourActorV3 && retryMatches.some((entry, index) => entry.retryOrdinal !== index + 1)) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: retry ordinals must be contiguous from 1`);
    const attempts = [...baseMatches, ...retryMatches];
    relevant.push(...attempts);
    observedContract.push(...attempts.map((entry) => ({ ...expected, taskName: entry.taskName, retryOrdinal: entry.retryOrdinal || 0 })));
    for (const entry of attempts) {
      if (!entry.receiverThreadId) failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: missing receiver thread id`);
      if (entry.forkTurns !== "none") failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: fork_turns must be none`);
      const runtimeKey = expected.scope === "epic" ? "epic-process-judge" : expected.control;
      const runtimeProfile = expectedSession.actorRuntimeProfiles?.[runtimeKey];
      if (runtimeProfile && (entry.model !== runtimeProfile.model
        || entry.reasoningEffort !== runtimeProfile.reasoningEffort)) {
        failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: runtime profile must be ${runtimeProfile.model}/${runtimeProfile.reasoningEffort}`);
      }
      if (!entry.parentFinalText) failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: missing parent-delivered FINAL_ANSWER`);
      if (fourActorV3 && entry.retryOrdinal
        && !new RegExp(`\\bREPAIR_CYCLE=${entry.retryOrdinal}\\b`).test(entry.parentFinalText)) {
        failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: v3 retry must bind REPAIR_CYCLE=${entry.retryOrdinal}`);
      }
    }
    if (expected.control === "atdd" && baseMatches.length === 1 && legacyPolicy) {
      const accepted = attempts.at(-1);
      if (!actorResultIs(accepted.parentFinalText, "PASS")) {
        failures.push(`${accepted.taskName}: legacy ATDD result is not PASS`);
      }
      acceptedActors.push({ ...expected, taskName: accepted.taskName, receiverThreadId: accepted.receiverThreadId });
    } else if (expected.control === "atdd" && baseMatches.length === 1) {
      const base = baseMatches[0];
      const basePassed = actorResultIs(base.parentFinalText, "PASS");
      const baseRevised = actorResultIs(base.parentFinalText, "REVISE");
      const adjudicationTaskName = `${expected.taskName}_adjudication1`;
      const correctionTaskName = `${expected.taskName}_correction1`;
      const adjudications = dispatches.filter((entry) => entry.taskName === adjudicationTaskName);
      const corrections = dispatches.filter((entry) => entry.taskName === correctionTaskName);
      for (const entry of [...adjudications, ...corrections]) {
        knownTaskNames.add(entry.taskName);
        relevant.push(entry);
        if (!entry.receiverThreadId) failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: missing receiver thread id`);
        if (entry.forkTurns !== "none") failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: fork_turns must be none`);
        if (!entry.parentFinalText) failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: missing parent-delivered FINAL_ANSWER`);
        const profileKey = entry.taskName === adjudicationTaskName ? "process-judge" : "atdd";
        const profile = expectedSession.actorRuntimeProfiles?.[profileKey];
        if (profile && (entry.model !== profile.model || entry.reasoningEffort !== profile.reasoningEffort)) {
          failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: runtime profile must be ${profile.model}/${profile.reasoningEffort}`);
        }
      }
      if (basePassed) {
        if (adjudications.length || corrections.length) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: PASS must not create ATDD correction work`);
        acceptedActors.push({ ...expected, taskName: base.taskName, receiverThreadId: base.receiverThreadId });
      } else if (baseRevised) {
        if (adjudications.length !== 1) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: REVISE requires exactly one independent adjudication`);
        if (adjudications.length === 1) {
          const adjudication = adjudications[0];
          const disposition = adjudication.parentFinalText.match(/\bATDD_ADJUDICATION=(OVERRULE|UPHOLD)\b/)?.[1] || "";
          if (!actorResultIs(adjudication.parentFinalText, "PASS") || !disposition) {
            failures.push(`${adjudicationTaskName}: adjudication must PASS with ATDD_ADJUDICATION=OVERRULE or UPHOLD`);
          }
          observedContract.push({
            scope: expected.scope,
            control: "atdd-adjudication",
            persona: "test-reviewer",
            retryable: false,
            taskName: adjudicationTaskName,
          });
          if (disposition === "OVERRULE") {
            if (corrections.length) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: overruled REVISE must not create a correction actor`);
            acceptedActors.push({ ...expected, taskName: adjudicationTaskName, receiverThreadId: adjudication.receiverThreadId });
          }
          if (disposition === "UPHOLD") {
            if (corrections.length !== 1) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: upheld REVISE requires exactly one correction actor`);
            if (corrections.length === 1) {
              const correction = corrections[0];
              if (!actorResultIs(correction.parentFinalText, "PASS")) failures.push(`${correctionTaskName}: correction result is not PASS`);
              correctionBindings.push({
                taskName: correctionTaskName,
                sourceTaskName: expected.taskName,
                findingsSha256: sha256(base.parentFinalText),
              });
              observedContract.push({
                scope: expected.scope,
                control: "atdd-correction",
                persona: "test-author",
                retryable: false,
                taskName: correctionTaskName,
              });
              acceptedActors.push({ ...expected, taskName: correctionTaskName, receiverThreadId: correction.receiverThreadId });
            }
          }
        }
      } else {
        failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: ATDD result must be PASS or REVISE`);
      }
    } else if (attempts.length) {
      const accepted = attempts[attempts.length - 1];
      if (!legacyPolicy && dispatchResult(accepted, expected.control) !== "PASS") failures.push(`${accepted.taskName}: final actor result is not PASS`);
      if (legacyPolicy && !actorResultIs(accepted.parentFinalText, "PASS")) failures.push(`${accepted.taskName}: legacy actor result is not PASS`);
      for (const superseded of legacyPolicy ? [] : attempts.slice(0, -1)) {
        const supersededResult = dispatchResult(superseded, expected.control);
        if (fourActorV3 && ["code-review", "patch-assurance"].includes(expected.control)) {
          if (!["PASS", "REVISE"].includes(supersededResult)) failures.push(`${superseded.taskName}: retry requires a valid prior typed reviewer result`);
        } else if (supersededResult !== "REVISE") {
          failures.push(`${superseded.taskName}: retry requires prior typed reviewer REVISE`);
        }
      }
      acceptedActors.push({ ...expected, taskName: accepted.taskName, receiverThreadId: accepted.receiverThreadId });
    }
  }
  const conditionalJudges = [];
  if (fourActorV3) {
    for (const scope of [...new Set(expectedContract.map((entry) => entry.scope).filter((entry) => entry !== "epic"))]) {
      const taskName = `acef_${normalizedActorToken(scope)}_process_judge`;
      const matches = dispatches.filter((entry) => entry.taskName === taskName);
      knownTaskNames.add(taskName);
      if (matches.length > 1) failures.push(`${taskName}: conditional story judge may spawn at most once`);
      if (matches.length === 1) {
        const entry = matches[0];
        relevant.push(entry);
        if (!entry.receiverThreadId) failures.push(`${taskName}: missing receiver thread id`);
        if (entry.forkTurns !== "none") failures.push(`${taskName}: fork_turns must be none`);
        if (!entry.parentFinalText) failures.push(`${taskName}: missing parent-delivered FINAL_ANSWER`);
        const judgeProfile = expectedSession.actorRuntimeProfiles?.["process-judge"];
        if (judgeProfile && (entry.model !== judgeProfile.model || entry.reasoningEffort !== judgeProfile.reasoningEffort)) {
          failures.push(`${taskName}: runtime profile must be ${judgeProfile.model}/${judgeProfile.reasoningEffort}`);
        }
        const normalizedTrigger = conditionalJudgeTrigger(entry.parentFinalText, expectedSession.cwd, taskName);
        if (!actorResultIs(entry.parentFinalText, "PASS")
          || !["ambiguity", "waiver", "evidence-conflict", "gate-anomaly"].includes(normalizedTrigger)) {
          failures.push(`${taskName}: conditional judge must PASS with an allowed JUDGE_TRIGGER`);
        }
        const actor = { scope, control: "process-judge", persona: "process-judge", retryable: false, taskName };
        observedContract.push(actor);
        acceptedActors.push({ ...actor, receiverThreadId: entry.receiverThreadId });
        conditionalJudges.push({ taskName, scope, trigger: normalizedTrigger });
      }
    }
  }
  const unexpected = dispatches.filter((entry) => !knownTaskNames.has(entry.taskName));
  if (unexpected.length && expectedSession.allowUnexpectedActors !== true) {
    failures.push(`unexpected lifecycle/closeout actors: ${unexpected.map((entry) => entry.taskName).join(", ")}`);
  }
  if (expectedSession.allowUnexpectedActors === true) {
    for (const entry of unexpected) {
      entry.auxiliary = true;
      if (!entry.receiverThreadId) failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: auxiliary actor receiver thread id missing`);
      if (entry.forkTurns !== "none") failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: auxiliary actor fork_turns must be none`);
      if (!entry.parentFinalText) failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: auxiliary actor parent-delivered FINAL_ANSWER missing`);
      if (["REVISE", "FAIL", "BLOCKED", "REPLAN"].includes(actorResultFromText(entry.parentFinalText))) {
        failures.push(`${entry.taskName}: auxiliary actor returned a terminal non-success result`);
      }
    }
  }
  const allDispatches = [...relevant, ...(expectedSession.allowUnexpectedActors === true ? unexpected : [])];
  const infrastructureRetryCount = dispatches.filter((entry) => /_infra_retry[1-9]\d*$/.test(entry.taskName)).length;
  const receiverIds = allDispatches.map((entry) => entry.receiverThreadId).filter(Boolean);
  if (new Set(receiverIds).size !== receiverIds.length) failures.push("lifecycle actors do not have distinct receiver thread ids");
  const repairCyclesByScope = {};
  const storyDeliverySeconds = {};
  const developerReactivations = [];
  const initialReviewPairs = [];
  let lifecycleIntegration = null;
  let storyTimingComplete = true;
  if (fourActorV3) {
    for (const scope of [...new Set(expectedContract.map((entry) => entry.scope).filter((entry) => entry !== "epic"))]) {
      const repairEntries = observedContract.filter((entry) => entry.scope === scope
        && ["code-review", "patch-assurance"].includes(entry.control) && Number(entry.retryOrdinal || 0) > 0);
      const ordinals = [...new Set(repairEntries.map((entry) => Number(entry.retryOrdinal)))].sort((left, right) => left - right);
      repairCyclesByScope[scope] = ordinals.length;
      if (ordinals.some((ordinal, index) => ordinal !== index + 1)) failures.push(`${scope}: repair-cycle ordinals must be contiguous from 1`);
      if (ordinals.length > 2) failures.push(`${scope}: third repair cycle requires REPLAN/SPLIT`);
      const developerLogicalTaskName = expectedContract.find((entry) => entry.scope === scope && entry.control === "development")?.taskName;
      const developerTaskName = relevant.find((entry) => entry.taskName === developerLogicalTaskName
        || entry.logicalTaskName === developerLogicalTaskName)?.taskName;
      for (const ordinal of ordinals) {
        const cycleEntries = repairEntries.filter((entry) => entry.retryOrdinal === ordinal);
        if (!cycleEntries.some((entry) => entry.control === "patch-assurance")) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: repair cycle ${ordinal} must rerun Patch Assurance on the repaired final tree`);
        }
        const retryDispatches = cycleEntries.map((entry) => relevant.find((dispatch) => dispatch.taskName === entry.taskName)).filter(Boolean);
        const priorPairs = cycleEntries.map((entry) => {
          const candidates = observedContract.filter((candidate) => candidate.scope === scope
            && candidate.control === entry.control && Number(candidate.retryOrdinal || 0) < ordinal);
          const prior = candidates.sort((left, right) => Number(right.retryOrdinal || 0) - Number(left.retryOrdinal || 0))[0];
          return { entry, dispatch: prior ? relevant.find((dispatch) => dispatch.taskName === prior.taskName) : null };
        });
        const priorDispatches = priorPairs.map((entry) => entry.dispatch).filter(Boolean);
        const priorFinishes = priorDispatches.map((entry) => Date.parse(entry.finalDeliveredAt || ""));
        const retryStarts = retryDispatches.map((entry) => Date.parse(entry.spawnedAt || ""));
        const orderedTimestamps = priorFinishes.length === cycleEntries.length && retryStarts.length === cycleEntries.length
          && priorFinishes.every(Number.isFinite) && retryStarts.every(Number.isFinite);
        if (!developerTaskName || !orderedTimestamps) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: repair cycle ${ordinal} cannot prove developer reactivation ordering`);
          continue;
        }
        const afterReviewerAt = Math.max(...priorFinishes);
        const beforeRetryAt = Math.min(...retryStarts);
        const matchingFollowups = followups.filter((entry) => {
          const target = String(entry.target || "").split("/").filter(Boolean).at(-1) || "";
          const calledAt = Date.parse(entry.calledAt || "");
          return target === developerTaskName && Number.isFinite(calledAt)
            && calledAt > afterReviewerAt && calledAt < beforeRetryAt;
        });
        if (matchingFollowups.length !== 1) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: repair cycle ${ordinal} requires exactly one followup_task to original developer`);
          continue;
        }
        boundFollowupCallIds.add(matchingFollowups[0].callId);
        const followupAt = Date.parse(matchingFollowups[0].calledAt);
        const repairedFinals = [...(completedAuthors.get(`/root/${developerTaskName}`) || []), ...(completedAuthors.get(developerTaskName) || [])]
          .filter((entry) => {
            const deliveredAt = Date.parse(entry.deliveredAt || "");
            return Number.isFinite(deliveredAt) && deliveredAt > followupAt && deliveredAt < beforeRetryAt
              && /Message Type:\s*FINAL_ANSWER/i.test(entry.content)
              && new RegExp(`\\bREPAIR_CYCLE=${ordinal}\\b`).test(entry.content)
              && actorResultIs(entry.content, "PASS");
          });
        if (repairedFinals.length !== 1) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: repair cycle ${ordinal} requires one repaired Developer FINAL_ANSWER before reviewer retries`);
          continue;
        }
        const repairReceiptPath = repairedFinals[0].content.match(/^REPAIR_RECEIPT_PATH=(.+?)\s*$/m)?.[1]?.trim() || "";
        const repairReceiptSha256 = repairedFinals[0].content.match(/^REPAIR_RECEIPT_SHA256=([a-f0-9]{64})\s*$/m)?.[1] || "";
        if (!/^docs\/ai\/repairs\/[^/]+\.json$/.test(repairReceiptPath) || !repairReceiptSha256) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: repair cycle ${ordinal} Developer FINAL_ANSWER lacks a typed repair receipt binding`);
          continue;
        }
        let productionRepair = false;
        if (expectedSession.cwd) {
          try {
            const receipt = installedStateParser(expectedSession.cwd)
              .parseDeveloperRepair(path.resolve(expectedSession.cwd, repairReceiptPath));
            const changed = execute("git", ["diff", "--name-only", receipt.preCommit, receipt.postCommit, "--"], expectedSession.cwd);
            productionRepair = changed.status === 0 && changed.stdout.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)
              .some((filePath) => !/^(?:tests?|spec)(?:\/|$)/i.test(filePath) && !isPilotHarnessPath(filePath));
          } catch {}
        }
        for (const pair of priorPairs.filter((entry) => entry.entry.control === "code-review")) {
          const priorResult = pair.dispatch ? (expectedSession.cwd
            ? reviewerResultFromReport(expectedSession.cwd, pair.dispatch.taskName)
            : actorResultFromText(pair.dispatch.parentFinalText)) : "";
          if (priorResult !== "REVISE" && !productionRepair) {
            failures.push(`${scope}: repair cycle ${ordinal} Code Review retry requires prior REVISE or a production repair`);
          }
        }
        developerReactivations.push({
          scope,
          repairCycle: ordinal,
          developerTaskName,
          developerSessionId: expectedSession.cwd ? (() => {
            try {
              return installedStateParser(expectedSession.cwd)
                .parseActorRecord(path.join(expectedSession.cwd, "docs", "ai", "actors", `${developerTaskName}.json`)).sessionId || null;
            } catch { return null; }
          })() : null,
          developerReceiverThreadId: relevant.find((entry) => entry.taskName === developerTaskName)?.receiverThreadId || null,
          followupCallId: matchingFollowups[0].callId,
          calledAt: matchingFollowups[0].calledAt,
          completedAt: repairedFinals[0].deliveredAt,
          repairedFinalSha256: sha256(repairedFinals[0].content),
          repairReceiptPath,
          repairReceiptSha256,
        });
      }
      for (let index = 1; index < ordinals.length; index += 1) {
        const priorTasks = new Set(repairEntries.filter((entry) => entry.retryOrdinal === ordinals[index - 1]).map((entry) => entry.taskName));
        const nextTasks = new Set(repairEntries.filter((entry) => entry.retryOrdinal === ordinals[index]).map((entry) => entry.taskName));
        const priorFinishes = relevant.filter((entry) => priorTasks.has(entry.taskName))
          .map((entry) => Date.parse(entry.finalDeliveredAt || "")).filter(Number.isFinite);
        const nextStarts = relevant.filter((entry) => nextTasks.has(entry.taskName))
          .map((entry) => Date.parse(entry.spawnedAt || "")).filter(Number.isFinite);
        if (priorFinishes.length && nextStarts.length && Math.max(...priorFinishes) > Math.min(...nextStarts)) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: repair cycles ${ordinals[index - 1]} and ${ordinals[index]} overlap`);
        }
      }
      const initialReviewDispatches = ["code-review", "patch-assurance"].map((control) => {
        const taskName = expectedContract.find((entry) => entry.scope === scope && entry.control === control)?.taskName;
        return relevant.find((entry) => entry.taskName === taskName || entry.logicalTaskName === taskName);
      });
      const reviewStarts = initialReviewDispatches.map((entry) => Date.parse(entry?.spawnedAt || ""));
      const reviewFinishes = initialReviewDispatches.map((entry) => Date.parse(entry?.finalDeliveredAt || ""));
      const concurrent = initialReviewDispatches.every(Boolean) && reviewStarts.every(Number.isFinite)
        && reviewFinishes.every(Number.isFinite) && Math.max(...reviewStarts) < Math.min(...reviewFinishes);
      if (!concurrent) failures.push(`${scope}: initial Code Review and Patch Assurance were not dispatched concurrently before either result`);
      initialReviewPairs.push({
        scope,
        concurrent,
        taskNames: initialReviewDispatches.map((entry) => entry?.taskName || null),
        spawnedAt: initialReviewDispatches.map((entry) => entry?.spawnedAt || null),
        completedAt: initialReviewDispatches.map((entry) => entry?.finalDeliveredAt || null),
      });
    }
    const unexpectedFollowups = followups.filter((entry) => !boundFollowupCallIds.has(entry.callId));
    if (unexpectedFollowups.length) {
      failures.push(`unexpected or unbound followup_task calls: ${unexpectedFollowups.map((entry) => entry.callId || entry.target).join(", ")}`);
    }
    const totalActorInvocations = relevant.length + infrastructureRetryCount + followups.length;
    if (totalActorInvocations > Number(expectedSession.maximumActorInvocations || 21)) {
      failures.push(`actor invocation budget exceeded: ${totalActorInvocations}/${expectedSession.maximumActorInvocations || 21}`);
    }
    for (const scope of [...new Set(expectedContract.map((entry) => entry.scope).filter((entry) => entry !== "epic"))]) {
      const taskNames = new Set(observedContract.filter((entry) => entry.scope === scope).map((entry) => entry.taskName));
      const storyDispatches = relevant.filter((entry) => taskNames.has(entry.taskName));
      const starts = storyDispatches.map((entry) => Date.parse(entry.spawnedAt || "")).filter(Number.isFinite);
      const finishes = storyDispatches.map((entry) => Date.parse(entry.finalDeliveredAt || "")).filter(Number.isFinite);
      if (!storyDispatches.length || starts.length !== storyDispatches.length || finishes.length !== storyDispatches.length) {
        storyTimingComplete = false;
        failures.push(`${scope}: story delivery timestamps are incomplete`);
      } else {
        storyDeliverySeconds[scope] = Math.round((Math.max(...finishes) - Math.min(...starts)) / 100) / 10;
      }
    }
    if (expectedSession.lifecycleIntegrationArgv) {
      const storyFinishedAt = relevant.filter((entry) => expectedContract.some((expected) => expected.scope !== "epic"
        && (entry.taskName === expected.taskName || entry.logicalTaskName === expected.taskName)))
        .map((entry) => entry.finalDeliveredAt).filter(Boolean).sort().at(-1) || null;
      const epicJudgeTaskName = expectedContract.find((entry) => entry.scope === "epic" && entry.control === "process-judge")?.taskName;
      const epicJudgeStartedAt = relevant.find((entry) => entry.taskName === epicJudgeTaskName
        || entry.logicalTaskName === epicJudgeTaskName)?.spawnedAt || null;
      lifecycleIntegration = parseLifecycleIntegrationEvidence(sessionText, expectedSession.lifecycleIntegrationArgv,
        storyFinishedAt, epicJudgeStartedAt);
      failures.push(...lifecycleIntegration.failures);
    }
  }
  return {
    ok: failures.length === 0,
    threadId,
    expectedActorCount: expectedContract.length,
    observedActorCount: relevant.length,
    frozenMandatoryActorCount: expectedContract.length,
    unexpectedActorCount: unexpected.length,
    closeoutCreatedMandatoryChains: unexpected.filter((entry) => /closeout|coverage|trace|stat|quality/i.test(entry.taskName)).length,
    correctionBindings,
    conditionalJudges,
    repairCyclesByScope,
    storyDeliverySeconds,
    storyTimingComplete,
    developerReactivations,
    initialReviewPairs,
    lifecycleIntegration,
    followupInvocationCount: fourActorV3 ? followups.length : 0,
    infrastructureRetryCount,
    infrastructureFailureReceipts,
    totalActorInvocations: relevant.length + infrastructureRetryCount + (fourActorV3 ? followups.length : 0),
    dispatches: allDispatches,
    observedDispatches: dispatches,
    actorContract: observedContract,
    dispatchTraceContract: [...observedContract, ...unexpected.map((entry) => inferAuxiliaryDispatch(entry, expectedContract)).filter(Boolean)],
    acceptedActors,
    failures,
    sessionSha256: sha256(sessionText),
    sessionStartedAt: sessionMeta?.timestamp || null,
    sessionClientVersion: sessionMeta?.cli_version || null,
    sessionCwd: sessionMeta?.cwd || null,
  };
}

function inferAuxiliaryDispatch(dispatch, expectedContract) {
  const token = normalizedActorToken(dispatch.taskName);
  const controls = [
    ["patch-assurance", /patch_assurance/],
    ["verify-patch", /verify_patch/],
    ["test-review", /test_review/],
    ["code-review", /code_review|reviewer/],
    ["process-judge", /process_judge/],
    ["development", /development|dev_story|developer/],
    ["atdd", /atdd/],
  ];
  const control = controls.find(([, pattern]) => pattern.test(token))?.[0];
  if (!control) return null;
  const scopes = [...new Set(expectedContract.map((entry) => entry.scope))];
  const scope = scopes.find((entry) => token.includes(normalizedActorToken(entry))) || (/epic/.test(token) ? "epic" : null);
  if (!scope) return null;
  const retryOrdinal = Number(token.match(/retry_?(\d+)$/)?.[1] || 0);
  return {
    scope,
    control,
    persona: "legacy-auxiliary",
    retryable: retryOrdinal === 1,
    retryOrdinal,
    auxiliary: true,
    taskName: dispatch.taskName,
  };
}

function correctionSessionWrites(sessionText, repoRoot) {
  const paths = [];
  const unsafeShellMutations = [];
  const unsafeDelegations = [];
  for (const line of String(sessionText || "").split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)) {
    let event;
    try { event = JSON.parse(line); } catch { continue; }
    const payload = event.payload || {};
    if (event.type !== "response_item" || !["function_call", "custom_tool_call"].includes(payload.type)) continue;
    const rawArguments = String(payload.arguments || payload.input || "");
    const normalizedArguments = rawArguments.replaceAll("\\n", "\n").replaceAll('\\"', '"');
    let args = {};
    try { args = JSON.parse(rawArguments || "{}"); } catch {}
    const name = String(payload.name || "");
    if (payload.type === "custom_tool_call" && name === "exec") {
      const allowedNestedTools = new Set(["apply_patch", "exec_command", "update_plan"]);
      const nestedTools = [...rawArguments.matchAll(/\btools\.([A-Za-z0-9_]+)\s*\(/g)].map((match) => match[1]);
      const bareToolReferences = [...rawArguments.matchAll(/\btools\b/g)].length - nestedTools.length;
      if (bareToolReferences > 0 || nestedTools.some((tool) => !allowedNestedTools.has(tool))) {
        unsafeShellMutations.push(`unrecognized custom tool access: ${rawArguments}`);
      }
    }
    if (payload.namespace === "collaboration" && /spawn_agent/i.test(name)) {
      unsafeDelegations.push(name);
    }
    if (/apply_patch/i.test(name) || /tools\.apply_patch\s*\(/.test(rawArguments)) {
      const patchText = String(args.input || args.patch || normalizedArguments);
      let observedPatchPaths = 0;
      for (const match of patchText.matchAll(/^\*\*\* (?:Add|Update|Delete) File:\s+(.+?)\s*$/gm)) {
        paths.push(path.resolve(repoRoot, match[1]));
        observedPatchPaths += 1;
      }
      if (observedPatchPaths === 0) unsafeShellMutations.push(`unobservable apply_patch: ${rawArguments}`);
    }
    if (/write|edit|notebook/i.test(name)) {
      const target = args.file_path || args.filePath || args.path || args.notebook_path;
      if (target) paths.push(path.resolve(repoRoot, target));
    }
    if (/exec_command|shell|bash/i.test(name) || /tools\.exec_command\s*\(/.test(rawArguments)) {
      const commands = extractCorrectionShellCommands(args, rawArguments);
      if (!commands.length) unsafeShellMutations.push(rawArguments);
      for (const command of commands) {
        if (!isAllowedCorrectionShellCommand(command)) unsafeShellMutations.push(command);
        paths.push(...reviewerPathsFromCompletionCommand(command, repoRoot));
      }
    }
  }
  return { paths: [...new Set(paths)], unsafeShellMutations, unsafeDelegations };
}

function canonicalReviewResultActor(command) {
  const normalized = String(command || "").trim();
  const prefix = /^(?:\.acef\/bin\/)?acef-state\s+review-result\s+--repo\s+\.\s+--actor\s+([A-Za-z0-9._-]+)(?:\s+--model\s+[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\s+--effort\s+(?:low|medium|high|xhigh|max))?\s+--verdict\s+(?:PASS|REVISE|REPLAN)/;
  const actor = normalized.match(prefix)?.[1] || "";
  if (!actor) return "";
  const suffix = normalized.replace(prefix, "");
  const compatibility = /^(?:\s+--finding\s+[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+)*$/;
  const typed = /^(?:\s+--finding-id\s+[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\s+--finding-severity\s+(?:LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL)\s+--finding-reason\s+(?:'[^'\r\n]+'|"[^"\r\n]+"))*$/;
  return compatibility.test(suffix) || typed.test(suffix) ? actor : "";
}

function reviewerPathsFromCompletionCommand(command, repoRoot) {
  const normalized = String(command || "").trim();
  const compatibility = normalized.match(
    /^(?:\.acef\/bin\/)?acef-state\s+review-completion\s+--repo\s+\.\s+--artifact-path\s+(docs\/ai\/reports\/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\.json)\s+--actor\s+([A-Za-z0-9._-]+)$/,
  );
  if (compatibility) return [
    path.resolve(repoRoot, compatibility[1]),
    path.resolve(repoRoot, "docs", "ai", "actors", `${compatibility[2]}.json`),
  ];
  const canonicalActor = canonicalReviewResultActor(normalized);
  return canonicalActor ? [
    path.resolve(repoRoot, "docs", "ai", "reports", `${canonicalActor}.json`),
    path.resolve(repoRoot, "docs", "ai", "actors", `${canonicalActor}.json`),
  ] : [];
}

function parseReviewerCompletion(lastAgentMessage, repoRoot) {
  const text = String(lastAgentMessage || "");
  const reportPathValue = text.match(/^REVIEW_REPORT_PATH=(.+)$/m)?.[1]?.trim() || "";
  const reportSha256 = text.match(/^REVIEW_REPORT_SHA256=([a-f0-9]{64})$/m)?.[1] || "";
  const reportBase64 = text.match(/^REVIEW_REPORT_BASE64=([A-Za-z0-9+/=]+)$/m)?.[1] || "";
  const inputTree = text.match(/^REVIEW_INPUT_TREE=([a-f0-9]{40,64})$/m)?.[1] || "";
  if (!reportPathValue || !reportSha256 || !reportBase64 || !inputTree) {
    throw new Error("reviewer completion must include report path, sha256, base64 blob, and input tree");
  }
  if (path.isAbsolute(reportPathValue) || reportPathValue.split(/[\\/]/).includes("..")
    || !/^docs\/ai\/reports\/[^/]+\.json$/.test(reportPathValue.replaceAll(path.sep, "/"))) {
    throw new Error("reviewer completion report path is invalid");
  }
  const reportBytes = Buffer.from(reportBase64, "base64");
  if (!reportBytes.length || reportBytes.toString("base64") !== reportBase64) {
    throw new Error("reviewer completion report blob is not canonical base64");
  }
  if (sha256(reportBytes.toString("utf8")) !== reportSha256) {
    throw new Error("reviewer completion report blob/hash mismatch");
  }
  let report;
  try { report = JSON.parse(reportBytes.toString("utf8")); }
  catch { throw new Error("reviewer completion report blob is invalid JSON"); }
  return {
    reportPath: reportPathValue.replaceAll(path.sep, "/"),
    absoluteReportPath: path.resolve(repoRoot, reportPathValue),
    reportSha256,
    reportBase64,
    inputTree,
    report,
  };
}

function toolOutputText(payload) {
  const blocks = Array.isArray(payload?.output) ? payload.output : [payload?.output];
  const texts = blocks.flatMap((entry) => {
    if (typeof entry === "string") return [entry];
    if (entry && typeof entry === "object") return [entry.text, entry.output_text].filter((value) => typeof value === "string");
    return [];
  });
  const expanded = [...texts];
  for (const value of texts) {
    try {
      const parsed = JSON.parse(value);
      if (typeof parsed?.output === "string") expanded.push(parsed.output);
    } catch {}
  }
  return expanded.join("\n");
}

function reviewerCompletionFromSession(sessionText, repoRoot, actorName) {
  const rows = String(sessionText || "").split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean).flatMap((line) => {
    try { return [JSON.parse(line)]; } catch { return []; }
  });
  const matches = [];
  for (const row of rows) {
    const payload = row.payload || {};
    if (row.type !== "response_item" || !["function_call", "custom_tool_call"].includes(payload.type)) continue;
    const rawArguments = String(payload.arguments || payload.input || "");
    let args = {};
    try { args = JSON.parse(rawArguments || "{}"); } catch {}
    for (const command of extractCorrectionShellCommands(args, rawArguments)) {
      if (!/(?:^|\s)(?:\.acef\/bin\/)?acef-state\s+(?:review-result|review-completion)\b/.test(command)
        || !new RegExp(`(?:^|\\s)--actor\\s+${actorName.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&")}(?:\\s|$)`).test(command)) continue;
      const outputRow = rows.find((candidate) => candidate.type === "response_item"
        && candidate.payload?.type === `${payload.type}_output`
        && candidate.payload?.call_id === payload.call_id);
      if (!outputRow) throw new Error("review result command output is missing from child transcript");
      matches.push(parseReviewerCompletion(toolOutputText(outputRow.payload), repoRoot));
    }
  }
  if (matches.length !== 1) throw new Error(`reviewer must run exactly one machine-observed review result command; observed ${matches.length}`);
  return matches[0];
}

function codexSessionMetrics(sessionText) {
  const rows = String(sessionText || "").split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean).flatMap((line) => {
    try { return [JSON.parse(line)]; } catch { return []; }
  });
  const tokenRows = rows.filter((row) => row.type === "event_msg" && row.payload?.type === "token_count"
    && row.payload?.info?.total_token_usage);
  const total = tokenRows.at(-1)?.payload?.info?.total_token_usage || {};
  const toolCallIds = new Set();
  const commandTexts = [];
  rows.forEach((row, index) => {
    const payload = row.payload || {};
    if (row.type !== "response_item" || !["function_call", "custom_tool_call"].includes(payload.type)) return;
    toolCallIds.add(payload.call_id || payload.id || `${payload.name || "tool"}:${index}`);
    const rawArguments = String(payload.arguments || payload.input || "");
    let args = {};
    try { args = JSON.parse(rawArguments || "{}"); } catch {}
    if (/exec_command|shell|bash/i.test(String(payload.name || "")) || /tools\.exec_command\s*\(/.test(rawArguments)) {
      if (typeof args.cmd === "string") commandTexts.push(args.cmd);
      else if (typeof args.command === "string") commandTexts.push(args.command);
      else commandTexts.push(...extractCorrectionShellCommands(args, rawArguments));
    }
  });
  return {
    input_tokens: Number(total.input_tokens || 0),
    cached_input_tokens: Number(total.cached_input_tokens || 0),
    output_tokens: Number(total.output_tokens || 0),
    model_cycles: tokenRows.length,
    tool_calls: toolCallIds.size,
    commandText: commandTexts.join("\n"),
  };
}

function v3AtddEvidenceCommandObserved(sessionText, taskName, story) {
  const commands = codexSessionMetrics(sessionText).commandText.split(/\r?\n/).map((entry) => entry.trim()).filter(Boolean);
  const actorPattern = taskName.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&");
  const storyPattern = story.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\]\\]/g, "\\$&");
  const matches = commands.filter((command) => new RegExp(
    `^(?:\\.acef/bin/)?acef-state\\s+evidence-run\\s+--repo\\s+\\.\\s+--id\\s+[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\\s+--kind\\s+runtime-test\\s+--actor\\s+${actorPattern}\\s+--story\\s+${storyPattern}(?:\\s+--model\\s+gpt-5\\.6-sol\\s+--effort\\s+high)?(?:\\s+--satisfies\\s+[A-Za-z0-9._-]+)+\\s+--\\s+.+$`,
  ).test(command));
  return matches.length === 1;
}

function aggregateTeamMetrics(conductorMetrics, childMetrics) {
  return {
    input_tokens: Number(conductorMetrics.input_tokens || 0) + Number(childMetrics.input_tokens || 0),
    cached_input_tokens: Number(conductorMetrics.cached_input_tokens || 0) + Number(childMetrics.cached_input_tokens || 0),
    output_tokens: Number(conductorMetrics.output_tokens || 0) + Number(childMetrics.output_tokens || 0),
    model_cycles: Number(conductorMetrics.model_cycles || 0) + Number(childMetrics.model_cycles || 0),
    tool_calls: Number(conductorMetrics.tool_calls || 0) + Number(childMetrics.tool_calls || 0),
  };
}

function extractCorrectionShellCommands(args, rawArguments) {
  if (typeof args.cmd === "string") return [args.cmd];
  if (typeof args.command === "string") return [args.command];
  const source = String(rawArguments || "");
  const callCount = [...source.matchAll(/tools\.exec_command\s*\(/g)].length;
  const commands = [];
  for (const match of source.matchAll(/tools\.exec_command\s*\(\s*\{\s*(?:"(?:cmd|command)"|(?:cmd|command))\s*:\s*("(?:\\.|[^"\\])*")/g)) {
    try { commands.push(JSON.parse(match[1])); } catch { return []; }
  }
  return commands.length === callCount ? commands : [];
}

function hasUnsafeShellMetacharacter(command) {
  const source = String(command || "");
  let singleQuoted = false;
  let doubleQuoted = false;
  for (let index = 0; index < source.length; index += 1) {
    const character = source[index];
    if (character === "\n" || character === "\r") return true;
    if (singleQuoted) {
      if (character === "'") singleQuoted = false;
      continue;
    }
    if (character === "\\") {
      index += 1;
      continue;
    }
    if (character === "'" && !doubleQuoted) {
      singleQuoted = true;
      continue;
    }
    if (character === '"') {
      doubleQuoted = !doubleQuoted;
      continue;
    }
    if (character === "`" || (character === "$" && source[index + 1] === "(")) return true;
    if (!doubleQuoted && ";|&<>".includes(character)) return true;
  }
  return singleQuoted || doubleQuoted;
}

function isAllowedCorrectionShellCommand(command) {
  const normalized = String(command || "").trim();
  if (!normalized || hasUnsafeShellMetacharacter(normalized)) return false;
  if (/\bgit\s+(?:diff|show)\b.*(?:--ext-diff|--textconv|--output(?:=|\s)|-o(?:\s|$))/.test(normalized)) return false;
  if (/\brg\b.*(?:--pre|--pre-glob)\b/.test(normalized)) return false;
  if (canonicalReviewResultActor(normalized)) return true;
  return [
    /^git\s+status(?:\s+(?:--short|--branch|--porcelain(?:=v[12])?))*$/,
    /^git\s+show\s+[A-Za-z0-9_./:@{}^,+~-]+$/,
    /^git\s+diff(?:\s+(?:--stat|--name-only|--check|--cached|--staged|--|[A-Za-z0-9_./:@{}^,+~-]+))*$/,
    /^git\s+(?:rev-parse|ls-files)(?:\s+[A-Za-z0-9_./:@={}^,+~-]+)*$/,
    /^rg(?:\s+--?[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9-]*(?:=[A-Za-z0-9_./:@,+~-]+)?|\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+)+$/,
    /^sed\s+-n\s+['"]?\d+(?:,\d+)?p['"]?\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+$/,
    /^(?:cat|ls|wc|shasum|sha256sum)(?:\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+)+$/,
    /^php\s+artisan\s+test(?:\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+)*$/,
    /^vendor\/bin\/phpunit(?:\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+)*$/,
    /^(?:npm|pnpm|yarn)\s+test(?:\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+)*$/,
    /^npx\s+(?:vitest|playwright)\s+test(?:\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+)*$/,
    /^composer\s+test(?:\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+)*$/,
    /^test\s+(?:!\s+)?-(?:e|f|d|r)\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+$/,
    /^php\s+-l\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+$/,
    /^(?:\.acef\/bin\/)?acef-state\s+review-completion\s+--repo\s+\.\s+--artifact-path\s+docs\/ai\/reports\/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\.json\s+--actor\s+[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$/,
  ].some((pattern) => pattern.test(normalized));
}

function isAllowedReviewerShellCommand(command) {
  const normalized = String(command || "").trim();
  if (!normalized || hasUnsafeShellMetacharacter(normalized)) return false;
  if (/\bgit\s+(?:add|am|apply|checkout|clean|commit|mv|rebase|reset|restore|rm|switch)\b/.test(normalized)) return false;
  if (/\bgit\s+(?:diff|show)\b.*(?:--ext-diff|--textconv|--output(?:=|\s)|-o(?:\s|$))/.test(normalized)) return false;
  if (/\bgit\s+grep\b.*(?:--textconv|--open-files-in-pager(?:=|\s))/.test(normalized)) return false;
  if (/\brg\b.*(?:--pre|--pre-glob)\b/.test(normalized) || /\bsed\b.*(?:^|\s)-i(?:\s|$)/.test(normalized)) return false;
  if (canonicalReviewResultActor(normalized)) return true;
  return [
    /^(?:\.acef\/bin\/)?acef-state\s+capsule-show\s+--repo\s+\.\s+--id\s+[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$/,
    /^git\s+(?:status|show|diff|diff-tree|rev-parse|ls-files|ls-tree|log|cat-file|merge-base|grep)\b/,
    /^(?:rg|cat|ls|wc|head|tail|shasum|sha256sum|jq)\b/,
    /^sed\s+-n\b/,
    /^awk\s+['"]FNR<=\d+\s+\{print\}['"](?:\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+)+$/,
    /^php\s+artisan\s+test\b/,
    /^vendor\/bin\/phpunit\b/,
    /^(?:npm|pnpm|yarn)\s+test\b/,
    /^npx\s+(?:vitest|playwright)\s+test\b/,
    /^composer\s+test\b/,
    /^node\s+--check\b/,
    /^test\s+(?:!\s+)?-(?:e|f|d|r)\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+$/,
    /^php\s+-l\s+[^\s;|&<>`]+$/,
    /^(?:\.acef\/bin\/)?acef-state\s+review-completion\s+--repo\s+\.\s+--artifact-path\s+docs\/ai\/reports\/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\.json\s+--actor\s+[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$/,
  ].some((pattern) => pattern.test(normalized));
}

function isCorrectionArtifactPath(filePath, repoRoot) {
  const relative = path.relative(repoRoot, filePath).replaceAll(path.sep, "/");
  if (!relative || relative.startsWith("../") || path.isAbsolute(relative)) return false;
  if (/^(?:tests?|spec)(?:\/|$)/i.test(relative) && !/(?:^|\/)Benchmark[^/]*Test\.(?:php|js|ts|tsx)$/i.test(relative)) return true;
  return /^_bmad-output\/test-artifacts\//.test(relative)
    || /^docs\/ai\/reports\//.test(relative);
}

function validateCorrectionBinding(repoRoot, binding) {
  const recordPath = path.join(repoRoot, "docs", "ai", "corrections", `${binding.taskName}.json`);
  if (!fs.existsSync(recordPath)) return [`${binding.taskName}: durable correction binding missing`];
  let record;
  try { record = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(recordPath, "utf8")); }
  catch { return [`${binding.taskName}: durable correction binding is invalid JSON`]; }
  const failures = [];
  if (record.schema !== "acef.atdd-correction.v1") failures.push(`${binding.taskName}: correction binding schema mismatch`);
  if (record.sourceActorId !== binding.sourceTaskName) failures.push(`${binding.taskName}: correction source actor mismatch`);
  if (record.correctionActorId !== binding.taskName) failures.push(`${binding.taskName}: correction actor mismatch`);
  if (record.scope !== "test-artifacts-only") failures.push(`${binding.taskName}: correction scope is not test-artifacts-only`);
  if (record.findingsSha256 !== binding.findingsSha256) failures.push(`${binding.taskName}: correction findings hash mismatch`);
  if (!Array.isArray(record.allowedPaths) || !record.allowedPaths.length) failures.push(`${binding.taskName}: correction allowedPaths missing`);
  else {
    for (const entry of record.allowedPaths) {
      if (typeof entry !== "string" || /[*?\[\]{}]/.test(entry) || path.isAbsolute(entry) || entry.split(/[\\/]/).includes("..")
        || !isCorrectionArtifactPath(path.resolve(repoRoot, entry), repoRoot)) {
        failures.push(`${binding.taskName}: invalid correction allowedPath ${String(entry)}`);
      }
    }
  }
  return failures;
}

function loadCollaborationEvidence(rawPath, expectedContract, expectedSession = {}) {
  const rawText = fs.readFileSync(rawPath, "utf8");
  let threadId = null;
  for (const line of rawText.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)) {
    try { const event = JSON.parse(line); if (event.type === "thread.started") threadId = event.thread_id; } catch {}
  }
  const sessionPath = findCodexSessionTranscript(threadId);
  if (!sessionPath) return { ok: false, threadId, sessionPath: null, failures: ["Codex session transcript not found"] };
  const evidence = parseCollaborationEvidence(rawText, fs.readFileSync(sessionPath, "utf8"), expectedContract, expectedSession);
  const failures = [...evidence.failures];
  const dispatchTraceContract = [...(evidence.dispatchTraceContract || evidence.actorContract || [])];
  let typedAuxiliaryCloseoutChains = 0;
  const auxiliaryDispatches = (evidence.dispatches || []).filter((entry) => entry.auxiliary);
  if (auxiliaryDispatches.length) {
    try {
      const parser = installedStateParser(expectedSession.cwd);
      const actorDir = path.join(expectedSession.cwd, "docs", "ai", "actors");
      const actors = new Map();
      if (fs.existsSync(actorDir)) for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(actorDir).filter((name) => name.endsWith(".json"))) {
        const actor = parser.parseActorRecord(path.join(actorDir, entry));
        actors.set(actor.actorInstanceId, actor);
      }
      const phaseMap = {
        atdd: "atdd",
        development: "development",
        codereview: "code-review",
        patchassurance: "patch-assurance",
        verifypatch: "verify-patch",
        testreview: "test-review",
        processjudge: "process-judge",
      };
      for (const dispatch of auxiliaryDispatches) {
        const actor = actors.get(dispatch.taskName);
        if (!actor) {
          failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: auxiliary typed actor record missing`);
          continue;
        }
        const control = phaseMap[canonicalLifecyclePhase(actor.phase || actor.role)];
        if (control) {
          const inferredIndex = dispatchTraceContract.findIndex((entry) => entry.auxiliary && entry.taskName === dispatch.taskName);
          const typed = {
            scope: actor.story,
            control,
            persona: actor.role,
            retryable: false,
            retryOrdinal: 0,
            auxiliary: true,
            taskName: dispatch.taskName,
          };
          if (inferredIndex >= 0) dispatchTraceContract[inferredIndex] = typed;
          else dispatchTraceContract.push(typed);
        }
        if (/closeout|coverage|trace|stat|quality/i.test(`${actor.phase} ${actor.role}`)) typedAuxiliaryCloseoutChains += 1;
      }
    } catch (error) {
      failures.push(`auxiliary typed actor reconciliation failed: ${error.message}`);
    }
  }
  for (const binding of evidence.correctionBindings || []) failures.push(...validateCorrectionBinding(expectedSession.cwd, binding));
  const childSessions = [];
  const reviewerCompletions = [];
  for (const dispatch of evidence.dispatches || []) {
    const childPath = findCodexSessionTranscript(dispatch.receiverThreadId);
    if (!childPath) { failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: child session transcript missing`); continue; }
    const childText = fs.readFileSync(childPath, "utf8");
    let meta = null;
    let completion = null;
    for (const line of childText.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)) {
      try {
        const event = JSON.parse(line);
        if (event.type === "session_meta") meta = event.payload || null;
        if (event.type === "event_msg" && event.payload?.type === "task_complete") completion = event.payload;
      } catch {}
    }
    if (!meta || meta.id !== dispatch.receiverThreadId || meta.parent_thread_id !== threadId
      || meta.agent_path !== `/root/${dispatch.taskName}`
      || meta.source?.subagent?.thread_spawn?.parent_thread_id !== threadId) {
      failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: child session provenance mismatch`);
    }
    const lifecycleEntry = (evidence.dispatchTraceContract || evidence.actorContract || [])
      .find((entry) => entry.taskName === dispatch.taskName);
    if (expectedSession.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3" && lifecycleEntry?.control === "development"
      && !developerActorSessionBound(expectedSession.cwd, dispatch.taskName, meta?.agent_path)) {
      failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: Developer actor sessionId does not bind the canonical spawn identity`);
    }
    if (expectedSession.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3" && lifecycleEntry?.control === "atdd") {
      let actor = null;
      try {
        actor = installedStateParser(expectedSession.cwd)
          .parseActorRecord(path.join(expectedSession.cwd, "docs", "ai", "actors", `${dispatch.taskName}.json`));
      } catch {}
      if (!actor || actor.sessionId !== meta?.agent_path || actor.role !== "test-author"
        || canonicalLifecyclePhase(actor.phase) !== "atdd") {
        failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: ATDD actor record was not atomically created by its canonical child session`);
      }
      if (!v3AtddEvidenceCommandObserved(childText, dispatch.taskName, lifecycleEntry.scope)) {
        failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: child transcript must contain exactly one canonical runtime-test evidence-run command`);
      }
    }
    const machineCarriedReviewer = expectedSession.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3"
      && ["code-review", "patch-assurance"].includes(lifecycleEntry?.control);
    if (!completion) failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: child task_complete missing`);
    else {
      const parentResult = actorResultFromText(dispatch.parentFinalText);
      const childResult = actorResultFromText(completion.last_agent_message);
      if (machineCarriedReviewer) {
        // The validated report verdict and review-completion receipt are the single typed reviewer result channel.
      } else if (dispatch.auxiliary && !parentResult && !childResult) {
        if (!dispatch.parentFinalText.includes(String(completion.last_agent_message || ""))) failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: auxiliary child/parent final answer mismatch`);
      } else if (!childResult || childResult !== parentResult) failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: child/parent actor result mismatch`);
    }
    if (/_atdd_(?:correction|adjudication)1$/.test(dispatch.taskName)) {
      const writes = correctionSessionWrites(childText, expectedSession.cwd);
      const adjudication = /_atdd_adjudication1$/.test(dispatch.taskName);
      let allowedCorrectionPaths = null;
      if (!adjudication) {
        try {
          const bindingPath = path.join(expectedSession.cwd, "docs", "ai", "corrections", `${dispatch.taskName}.json`);
          const binding = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(bindingPath, "utf8"));
          allowedCorrectionPaths = new Set((binding.allowedPaths || []).map((entry) => path.resolve(expectedSession.cwd, entry)));
          const spawnCommit = meta?.git?.commit_hash || "";
          const bindingRelative = path.relative(expectedSession.cwd, bindingPath).replaceAll(path.sep, "/");
          const committedBinding = spawnCommit
            ? execute("git", ["show", `${spawnCommit}:${bindingRelative}`], expectedSession.cwd)
            : { status: 1, stdout: "" };
          if (committedBinding.status !== 0 || sha256(committedBinding.stdout) !== sha256(fs.readFileSync(bindingPath, "utf8"))) {
            failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: correction binding was not committed unchanged before spawn`);
          }
        } catch {}
      }
      const forbidden = writes.paths.filter((entry) => adjudication
        ? !/^docs\/ai\/reports\//.test(path.relative(expectedSession.cwd, entry).replaceAll(path.sep, "/"))
        : !isCorrectionArtifactPath(entry, expectedSession.cwd) || !allowedCorrectionPaths?.has(entry));
      if (forbidden.length) failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: bounded ATDD actor wrote outside its allowed artifacts: ${forbidden.map((entry) => path.relative(expectedSession.cwd, entry)).join(", ")}`);
      if (writes.unsafeShellMutations.length) failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: bounded ATDD actor used an unscoped shell mutation`);
      if (writes.unsafeDelegations.length) failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: bounded ATDD actor delegated work`);
    }
    if (expectedSession.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3"
      && ["code-review", "patch-assurance"].includes(lifecycleEntry?.control)) {
      const writes = correctionSessionWrites(childText, expectedSession.cwd);
      const childCommands = codexSessionMetrics(childText).commandText.split(/\r?\n/).map((entry) => entry.trim()).filter(Boolean);
      const capsuleShowCommands = childCommands.filter((command) => /^(?:\.acef\/bin\/)?acef-state\s+capsule-show\s+--repo\s+\.\s+--id\s+[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$/.test(command));
      if (expectedSession.runtimeContract === "capsule-supervisor-v1" && capsuleShowCommands.length !== 1) {
        failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: reviewer must execute exactly one capsule-show command`);
      }
      let captured = null;
      try { captured = reviewerCompletionFromSession(childText, expectedSession.cwd, dispatch.taskName); }
      catch (error) { failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: ${error.message}`); }
      const allowedReportPath = captured?.absoluteReportPath || null;
      const allowedActorPath = path.resolve(expectedSession.cwd, "docs", "ai", "actors", `${dispatch.taskName}.json`);
      let actor = null;
      try {
        const parser = installedStateParser(expectedSession.cwd);
        actor = parser.parseActorRecord(path.join(expectedSession.cwd, "docs", "ai", "actors", `${dispatch.taskName}.json`));
      } catch {}
      const allowedWrites = new Set([allowedReportPath, allowedActorPath].filter(Boolean));
      const forbidden = writes.paths.filter((entry) => !allowedWrites.has(entry));
      if (forbidden.length) {
        failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: report-only reviewer wrote outside its bound report/actor handoff: ${forbidden.map((entry) => path.relative(expectedSession.cwd, entry)).join(", ")}`);
      }
      if (!allowedReportPath || !writes.paths.includes(allowedReportPath)) {
        failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: report-only reviewer did not create its bound typed report`);
      }
      if (!writes.paths.includes(allowedActorPath)) {
        failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: review-completion did not create its bound immutable actor record`);
      }
      const unsafeReviewerCommands = writes.unsafeShellMutations.filter((command) => !isAllowedReviewerShellCommand(command));
      if (unsafeReviewerCommands.length) failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: report-only reviewer used an unsafe or unobservable shell mutation`);
      if (writes.unsafeDelegations.length) failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: report-only reviewer delegated work`);
      if (captured) {
        if (!actor || actor.producedArtifactPath !== captured.reportPath
          || actor.producedArtifactHash !== captured.reportSha256 || actor.inputTree !== captured.inputTree) {
          failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: actor record does not bind the reviewer completion report blob/hash/input tree`);
        }
        if (!fs.existsSync(captured.absoluteReportPath)
          || sha256File(captured.absoluteReportPath) !== captured.reportSha256
          || fs.readFileSync(captured.absoluteReportPath, "utf8") !== Buffer.from(captured.reportBase64, "base64").toString("utf8")) {
          failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: reviewer completion report was replaced after child completion`);
        }
        if (expectedSession.runtimeContract === "capsule-supervisor-v1" && capsuleShowCommands.length === 1) {
          try {
            const capsuleId = capsuleShowCommands[0].match(/--id\s+([A-Za-z0-9._-]+)$/)[1];
            const capsulePath = path.join(expectedSession.cwd, "docs", "ai", "capsules", `${capsuleId}.json`);
            const capsule = installedStateParser(expectedSession.cwd).parseAssuranceCapsule(capsulePath);
            const report = installedStateParser(expectedSession.cwd).parseReviewReport(captured.absoluteReportPath);
            const expectedRole = lifecycleEntry.control;
            if (capsule.actorInstanceId !== dispatch.taskName || capsule.role !== expectedRole
              || capsule.inputTree !== captured.inputTree || report.capsulePath !== path.relative(expectedSession.cwd, capsulePath).replaceAll(path.sep, "/")
              || report.capsuleSha256 !== sha256File(capsulePath)) {
              failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: capsule-show/report actor, role, tree, or hash binding mismatch`);
            }
          } catch (error) {
            failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: invalid capsule-show binding: ${error.message}`);
          }
        }
        reviewerCompletions.push({
          taskName: dispatch.taskName,
          scope: lifecycleEntry.scope,
          control: lifecycleEntry.control,
          reportPath: captured.reportPath,
          reportSha256: captured.reportSha256,
          reportBase64: captured.reportBase64,
          inputTree: captured.inputTree,
          childSessionId: dispatch.receiverThreadId,
          childCompletedAt: completion?.completed_at || null,
        });
      }
    }
    const metrics = codexSessionMetrics(childText);
    childSessions.push({
      taskName: dispatch.taskName,
      threadId: dispatch.receiverThreadId,
      sessionSha256: sha256(childText),
      completedAt: completion?.completed_at || null,
      metrics,
    });
  }
  const selectedTaskNames = new Set((evidence.dispatches || []).map((entry) => entry.taskName));
  for (const dispatch of evidence.observedDispatches || []) {
    if (selectedTaskNames.has(dispatch.taskName) || !dispatch.receiverThreadId
      || !(evidence.observedDispatches || []).some((entry) => entry.taskName === `${dispatch.taskName}_infra_retry1`)) continue;
    const childPath = findCodexSessionTranscript(dispatch.receiverThreadId);
    if (!childPath) { failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: failed infrastructure invocation child transcript missing`); continue; }
    const childText = fs.readFileSync(childPath, "utf8");
    let meta = null;
    for (const line of childText.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)) {
      try { const event = JSON.parse(line); if (event.type === "session_meta") meta = event.payload || null; } catch {}
    }
    if (!meta || meta.id !== dispatch.receiverThreadId || meta.parent_thread_id !== threadId) {
      failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: failed infrastructure invocation provenance mismatch`);
    }
    const failedWrites = correctionSessionWrites(childText, expectedSession.cwd);
    if (failedWrites.paths.length || failedWrites.unsafeShellMutations.length || failedWrites.unsafeDelegations.length) {
      failures.push(`${dispatch.taskName}: failed infrastructure invocation is not proven zero-write`);
    }
    childSessions.push({
      taskName: dispatch.taskName,
      threadId: dispatch.receiverThreadId,
      sessionSha256: sha256(childText),
      completedAt: null,
      infrastructureFailed: true,
      metrics: codexSessionMetrics(childText),
    });
  }
  if (expectedSession.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3") {
    for (const pair of evidence.initialReviewPairs || []) {
      const completions = pair.taskNames.map((taskName) => reviewerCompletions.find((entry) => entry.taskName === taskName)).filter(Boolean);
      if (completions.length !== 2 || new Set(completions.map((entry) => entry.inputTree)).size !== 1) {
        failures.push(`${pair.scope}: concurrent initial reviewers do not bind one shared input tree`);
      }
    }
  }
  const childMetrics = childSessions.reduce((total, entry) => ({
    input_tokens: total.input_tokens + entry.metrics.input_tokens,
    cached_input_tokens: total.cached_input_tokens + entry.metrics.cached_input_tokens,
    output_tokens: total.output_tokens + entry.metrics.output_tokens,
    model_cycles: total.model_cycles + entry.metrics.model_cycles,
    tool_calls: total.tool_calls + entry.metrics.tool_calls,
    commandText: [total.commandText, entry.metrics.commandText].filter(Boolean).join("\n"),
  }), { input_tokens: 0, cached_input_tokens: 0, output_tokens: 0, model_cycles: 0, tool_calls: 0, commandText: "" });
  return {
    ...evidence,
    ok: failures.length === 0,
    failures,
    sessionPath,
    childSessions,
    childMetrics,
    reviewerCompletions,
    dispatchTraceContract,
    closeoutCreatedMandatoryChains: Math.max(evidence.closeoutCreatedMandatoryChains || 0, typedAuxiliaryCloseoutChains),
  };
}

function canonicalLifecyclePhase(value) {
  const token = normalizedActorToken(value).replace(/_/g, "");
  const aliases = { codereviewer: "codereview", reviewer: "codereview", patchassurancereviewer: "patchassurance", patchverifier: "verifypatch", testreviewer: "testreview", judge: "processjudge", epicprocessjudge: "processjudge" };
  return aliases[token] || token;
}

function parseHarnessWaitMetrics(sessionText, activeDeliverySeconds = 0, collaborationEvidence = {}) {
  const pending = new Map();
  const intervals = [];
  let waitCalls = 0;
  let invalidTimestampEvents = 0;
  for (const line of String(sessionText || "").split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)) {
    let event;
    try { event = JSON.parse(line); } catch { continue; }
    const timestamp = Date.parse(event.timestamp || "");
    const payload = event.payload || {};
    const waitCall = event.type === "response_item" && payload.type === "function_call"
      && payload.namespace === "collaboration" && payload.name === "wait_agent";
    const waitOutput = event.type === "response_item" && payload.type === "function_call_output" && pending.has(payload.call_id);
    if (!Number.isFinite(timestamp)) {
      if (waitCall || waitOutput) invalidTimestampEvents += 1;
      continue;
    }
    if (waitCall) {
      if (pending.has(payload.call_id)) invalidTimestampEvents += 1;
      pending.set(payload.call_id, timestamp);
      waitCalls += 1;
    }
    if (waitOutput) {
      const startedAt = pending.get(payload.call_id);
      if (timestamp >= startedAt) intervals.push([startedAt, timestamp]);
      else invalidTimestampEvents += 1;
      pending.delete(payload.call_id);
    }
  }
  intervals.sort((left, right) => left[0] - right[0]);
  const merged = [];
  for (const interval of intervals) {
    const previous = merged.at(-1);
    if (!previous || interval[0] > previous[1]) merged.push([...interval]);
    else previous[1] = Math.max(previous[1], interval[1]);
  }
  const seconds = Math.round(merged.reduce((total, [start, finish]) => total + finish - start, 0) / 100) / 10;
  const completions = new Map((collaborationEvidence.childSessions || []).map((entry) => [
    entry.taskName,
    Number(entry.completedAt) * 1000,
  ]));
  const actorIntervals = (collaborationEvidence.observedDispatches || collaborationEvidence.dispatches || [])
    .map((entry) => [Date.parse(entry.spawnedAt || ""), completions.get(entry.taskName)])
    .filter(([start, finish]) => Number.isFinite(start) && Number.isFinite(finish) && finish >= start)
    .sort((left, right) => left[0] - right[0]);
  let delegatedExecutionMs = 0;
  for (const [waitStart, waitFinish] of merged) {
    const overlaps = actorIntervals
      .map(([actorStart, actorFinish]) => [Math.max(waitStart, actorStart), Math.min(waitFinish, actorFinish)])
      .filter(([start, finish]) => finish > start)
      .sort((left, right) => left[0] - right[0]);
    const mergedOverlaps = [];
    for (const overlap of overlaps) {
      const previous = mergedOverlaps.at(-1);
      if (!previous || overlap[0] > previous[1]) mergedOverlaps.push([...overlap]);
      else previous[1] = Math.max(previous[1], overlap[1]);
    }
    delegatedExecutionMs += mergedOverlaps.reduce((total, [start, finish]) => total + finish - start, 0);
  }
  const delegatedExecutionSeconds = Math.round(delegatedExecutionMs / 100) / 10;
  const coordinationIdleSeconds = Math.round(Math.max(0, seconds - delegatedExecutionSeconds) * 10) / 10;
  return {
    waitCalls,
    completedWaitCalls: intervals.length,
    incompleteWaitCalls: pending.size,
    invalidTimestampEvents,
    measurementComplete: pending.size === 0 && invalidTimestampEvents === 0,
    seconds,
    share: activeDeliverySeconds > 0 ? Math.round((seconds / activeDeliverySeconds) * 10000) / 10000 : 0,
    delegatedExecutionSeconds,
    delegatedExecutionShare: activeDeliverySeconds > 0
      ? Math.round((delegatedExecutionSeconds / activeDeliverySeconds) * 10000) / 10000 : 0,
    coordinationIdleSeconds,
    coordinationIdleShare: activeDeliverySeconds > 0
      ? Math.round((coordinationIdleSeconds / activeDeliverySeconds) * 10000) / 10000 : 0,
  };
}

function lifecycleIntegrationCommand(argv) {
  if (!Array.isArray(argv) || !argv.length) return "";
  return argv[0] === "sh" && argv[1] === "-c" && argv.length === 3
    ? argv[2] : argv.join(" ");
}

function parseLifecycleIntegrationEvidence(sessionText, expectedArgv, afterStoryAt, beforeJudgeAt) {
  const expectedCommand = lifecycleIntegrationCommand(expectedArgv);
  const expectedShellWrapper = expectedArgv[0] === "sh" && expectedArgv[1] === "-c" && expectedArgv.length === 3
    ? `sh -c ${JSON.stringify(expectedArgv[2])}` : "";
  const calls = [];
  const outputs = new Map();
  for (const line of String(sessionText || "").split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)) {
    let row;
    try { row = JSON.parse(line); } catch { continue; }
    const payload = row.payload || {};
    if (row.type === "response_item" && ["function_call", "custom_tool_call"].includes(payload.type)) {
      const commands = extractCorrectionShellCommands({}, String(payload.arguments || payload.input || ""));
      let args = {};
      try { args = JSON.parse(payload.arguments || "{}"); } catch {}
      if (typeof args.cmd === "string") commands.push(args.cmd);
      if (typeof args.command === "string") commands.push(args.command);
      for (const command of new Set(commands)) if (command === expectedCommand || command === expectedShellWrapper) {
        calls.push({ callId: payload.call_id || payload.id || "", startedAt: row.timestamp || null, command });
      }
    }
    if (row.type === "response_item" && ["function_call_output", "custom_tool_call_output"].includes(payload.type)) {
      outputs.set(payload.call_id || payload.id || "", {
        finishedAt: row.timestamp || null,
        text: toolOutputText(payload),
      });
    }
  }
  const failures = [];
  if (calls.length !== 1) failures.push(`exact frozen lifecycle integration command invocations ${calls.length}/1`);
  const call = calls[0];
  const output = call ? outputs.get(call.callId) : null;
  const explicitExitCodes = output ? [...output.text.matchAll(/["']?exit_code["']?\s*:\s*(-?\d+)/gi)]
    .map((match) => Number(match[1])) : [];
  const otherExplicitExitCodes = output ? [...output.text.matchAll(/(?:Process exited with code|exit code)\s+(-?\d+)/gi)]
    .map((match) => Number(match[1])) : [];
  const successfulInnerExit = explicitExitCodes.length > 0 && explicitExitCodes.every((code) => code === 0)
    && otherExplicitExitCodes.every((code) => code === 0);
  const startedAt = Date.parse(call?.startedAt || "");
  const finishedAt = Date.parse(output?.finishedAt || "");
  const afterAt = Date.parse(afterStoryAt || "");
  const judgeAt = Date.parse(beforeJudgeAt || "");
  if (calls.length === 1 && (!output || !successfulInnerExit
    || ![startedAt, finishedAt, afterAt, judgeAt].every(Number.isFinite)
    || startedAt <= afterAt || finishedAt < startedAt || finishedAt >= judgeAt)) {
    failures.push("lifecycle integration command lacks a successful exit receipt after all story results and before Epic Judge dispatch");
  }
  return {
    ok: failures.length === 0,
    count: calls.length,
    expectedArgv,
    expectedCommand,
    commandSha256: sha256(JSON.stringify(expectedArgv)),
    callId: call?.callId || null,
    startedAt: call?.startedAt || null,
    finishedAt: output?.finishedAt || null,
    outputSha256: output ? sha256(output.text) : null,
    failures,
  };
}

function evaluatePilotBudgets(manifest, attempt, activeDeliverySeconds, actor, collaborationEvidence, commandTrace, harnessWait) {
  if (attempt.actorContractVersion !== "four-actor-v3") return { applicable: false, ok: true, failures: [] };
  const budget = manifest.promotionGates.budget;
  const failures = [];
  const actorInvocations = Number(collaborationEvidence.totalActorInvocations
    ?? collaborationEvidence.observedActorCount ?? 0);
  const infrastructureRetries = (collaborationEvidence.observedDispatches || collaborationEvidence.dispatches || [])
    .filter((entry) => /_infra_retry[1-9]\d*$/.test(entry.taskName));
  const infrastructureRetriesByInvocation = {};
  let invalidInfrastructureRetryOrdinal = false;
  for (const entry of infrastructureRetries) {
    const match = entry.taskName.match(/^(.*)_infra_retry([1-9]\d*)$/);
    if (!match || /_infra_retry[1-9]\d*$/.test(match[1])) {
      invalidInfrastructureRetryOrdinal = true;
      continue;
    }
    const invocation = match[1];
    const ordinal = Number(match[2]);
    const current = infrastructureRetriesByInvocation[invocation] || { count: 0, ordinals: [] };
    current.count += 1;
    current.ordinals.push(ordinal);
    infrastructureRetriesByInvocation[invocation] = current;
  }
  const maximumStoryRepairCycles = Math.max(0, ...Object.values(collaborationEvidence.repairCyclesByScope || {}).map(Number));
  const storyDeliverySeconds = collaborationEvidence.storyDeliverySeconds || {};
  if (actorInvocations > budget.maximumActorInvocations) failures.push(`actor invocations ${actorInvocations}/${budget.maximumActorInvocations}`);
  if (maximumStoryRepairCycles > budget.maximumRepairCyclesPerStory) failures.push(`repair cycles ${maximumStoryRepairCycles}/${budget.maximumRepairCyclesPerStory}`);
  if (infrastructureRetries.length > budget.maximumInfrastructureRetriesTotal) failures.push(`infrastructure retries ${infrastructureRetries.length}/${budget.maximumInfrastructureRetriesTotal}`);
  if (invalidInfrastructureRetryOrdinal) failures.push("infrastructure retry naming is invalid or nested");
  for (const [invocation, retries] of Object.entries(infrastructureRetriesByInvocation)) {
    const uniqueOrdinals = new Set(retries.ordinals);
    if (retries.count > budget.maximumInfrastructureRetriesPerInvocation
      || uniqueOrdinals.size !== retries.count
      || retries.ordinals.some((ordinal) => ordinal > budget.maximumInfrastructureRetriesPerInvocation)) {
      failures.push(`${invocation} infrastructure retries ${retries.count}/${budget.maximumInfrastructureRetriesPerInvocation}`);
    }
  }
  if (collaborationEvidence.storyTimingComplete === false) failures.push("story delivery timestamps are incomplete");
  for (const [scope, seconds] of Object.entries(storyDeliverySeconds)) {
    if (seconds > budget.maximumStoryActiveSeconds) failures.push(`${scope} active delivery ${seconds}s/${budget.maximumStoryActiveSeconds}s`);
  }
  if (activeDeliverySeconds > budget.maximumActiveDeliverySeconds) failures.push(`active delivery ${activeDeliverySeconds}s/${budget.maximumActiveDeliverySeconds}s`);
  if (actor.input_tokens > budget.maximumInputTokens) failures.push(`input tokens ${actor.input_tokens}/${budget.maximumInputTokens}`);
  if (Number.isInteger(budget.maximumModelCycles) && actor.model_cycles > budget.maximumModelCycles) {
    failures.push(`model cycles ${actor.model_cycles}/${budget.maximumModelCycles}`);
  }
  if (actor.tool_calls > budget.maximumToolCalls) failures.push(`tool calls ${actor.tool_calls}/${budget.maximumToolCalls}`);
  const coordinationIdleBudget = ["v33-measured", "capsule-supervisor-v1"].includes(budget.profileId);
  const measuredWaitSeconds = coordinationIdleBudget
    ? Number(harnessWait.coordinationIdleSeconds || 0) : harnessWait.seconds;
  const measuredWaitShare = coordinationIdleBudget
    ? Number(harnessWait.coordinationIdleShare || 0) : harnessWait.share;
  const waitLabel = coordinationIdleBudget ? "coordination idle wait" : "harness wait";
  if (measuredWaitSeconds > budget.maximumHarnessWaitSeconds) failures.push(`${waitLabel} ${measuredWaitSeconds}s/${budget.maximumHarnessWaitSeconds}s`);
  if (measuredWaitShare > budget.maximumHarnessWaitShare) failures.push(`${waitLabel} share ${measuredWaitShare}/${budget.maximumHarnessWaitShare}`);
  if (harnessWait.measurementComplete === false || Number(harnessWait.incompleteWaitCalls || 0) > 0) {
    failures.push("harness wait measurement is incomplete");
  }
  const broadSuiteInvocations = collaborationEvidence.lifecycleIntegration
    ? Number(collaborationEvidence.lifecycleIntegration.count || 0)
    : Number(commandTrace.counts?.broadSuite || 0);
  const requiredBroadSuiteInvocations = Number(manifest.promotionGates.process.maximumBroadSuiteInvocations);
  if (broadSuiteInvocations !== requiredBroadSuiteInvocations) {
    failures.push(`broad suites ${broadSuiteInvocations}/${requiredBroadSuiteInvocations}; v3 requires exactly one lifecycle broad suite at epic close`);
  }
  return {
    applicable: true,
    ok: failures.length === 0,
    targetMet: activeDeliverySeconds <= budget.targetActiveDeliverySeconds,
    storyTargetsMet: Object.values(storyDeliverySeconds).every((seconds) => seconds <= budget.targetStoryActiveSeconds),
    actorInvocations,
    baseActorCount: budget.baseActorCount,
    infrastructureRetries: infrastructureRetries.length,
    infrastructureRetriesByInvocation,
    maximumStoryRepairCycles,
    storyDeliverySeconds,
    activeDeliverySeconds,
    inputTokens: actor.input_tokens,
    modelCycles: actor.model_cycles,
    toolCalls: actor.tool_calls,
    broadSuiteInvocations,
    harnessWait,
    failures,
  };
}

function installedStateParser(clone) {
  const parserPath = path.join(clone, ".acef", "bin", "lib", "acef-state-parser.js");
  if (!fs.existsSync(parserPath)) throw new Error(`installed treatment state parser missing: ${parserPath}`);
  return require(parserPath);
}

function committedUnchangedAtHead(clone, filePath) {
  const absolute = path.resolve(filePath);
  const cloneReal = fs.realpathSync(clone);
  const lexicalRelative = path.relative(path.resolve(clone), absolute);
  if (!lexicalRelative || lexicalRelative.startsWith("..") || path.isAbsolute(lexicalRelative)) {
    return { ok: false, reason: "path escapes clone" };
  }
  if (!fs.existsSync(absolute)) return { ok: false, reason: "file is missing" };
  const stat = fs.lstatSync(absolute);
  if (stat.isSymbolicLink() || !stat.isFile()) return { ok: false, reason: "path is not a regular file" };
  const absoluteReal = fs.realpathSync(absolute);
  const realRelative = path.relative(cloneReal, absoluteReal);
  if (!realRelative || realRelative.startsWith("..") || path.isAbsolute(realRelative)) {
    return { ok: false, reason: "real path escapes clone" };
  }
  const relative = realRelative.replaceAll(path.sep, "/");
  if (execute("git", ["ls-files", "--error-unmatch", "--", relative], clone).status !== 0) {
    return { ok: false, reason: "file is not tracked" };
  }
  const staged = execute("git", ["ls-files", "--stage", "--", relative], clone);
  if (staged.status !== 0 || !/^100(?:644|755)\s+[a-f0-9]{40,64}\s+0\t/.test(staged.stdout)) {
    return { ok: false, reason: "HEAD path is not a regular tracked blob" };
  }
  if (execute("git", ["diff", "--quiet", "HEAD", "--", relative], clone).status !== 0) {
    return { ok: false, reason: "file differs from HEAD" };
  }
  const committed = cp.spawnSync("git", ["show", `HEAD:${relative}`], {
    cwd: clone, encoding: null, stdio: ["ignore", "pipe", "pipe"],
  });
  if (committed.status !== 0) {
    return { ok: false, reason: "file is not committed at HEAD" };
  }
  if (!Buffer.from(committed.stdout || []).equals(fs.readFileSync(absolute))) {
    return { ok: false, reason: "filesystem bytes do not match the committed blob" };
  }
  return { ok: true, relative };
}

function requireCommittedUnchanged(failures, scope, label, clone, filePath) {
  const result = committedUnchangedAtHead(clone, filePath);
  if (!result.ok) failures.push(`${scope}: ${label} ${result.reason}`);
}

function committedRedIsTestOnly(clone, commit) {
  const parent = execute("git", ["rev-parse", `${commit}^`], clone);
  if (parent.status !== 0) return false;
  const changed = execute("git", ["diff", "--name-only", parent.stdout.trim(), commit, "--"], clone);
  if (changed.status !== 0) return false;
  const paths = changed.stdout.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean);
  const testPaths = paths.filter((entry) => /^(?:tests?|spec)(?:\/|$)/i.test(entry));
  return testPaths.length > 0 && paths.every((entry) => /^(?:tests?|spec)(?:\/|$)/i.test(entry)
    || isPilotHarnessPath(entry));
}

function changedPathsFromCommit(clone, commit) {
  const changed = execute("git", ["diff", "--name-only", commit, "HEAD", "--"], clone);
  if (changed.status !== 0) return null;
  return changed.stdout.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean);
}

function validateFormalStoryClosePackage(scope, gate, clone, actorPaths, reportPaths, parser, allGates = []) {
  const failures = [];
  const gateById = new Map(allGates.map((entry) => [entry.gateId, entry]));
  gateById.set(gate.gateId, gate);
  const layers = [];
  const visited = new Set();
  for (let cursor = gate; cursor; ) {
    if (visited.has(cursor.gateId)) {
      failures.push(`${scope}: formal story-close repair chain contains a cycle`);
      return failures;
    }
    visited.add(cursor.gateId);
    layers.unshift(cursor);
    const priorGateId = cursor.repair?.priorGateId;
    if (!priorGateId) break;
    cursor = gateById.get(priorGateId);
    if (!cursor) {
      failures.push(`${scope}: formal story-close prior gate ${priorGateId} is missing`);
      return failures;
    }
  }
  const seenPaths = new Set();
  for (const layer of layers) {
    const packagePaths = [layer._recordPath];
    for (const actorId of Object.values(layer.actors || {})) {
      packagePaths.push(path.join(clone, "docs", "ai", "actors", `${actorId}.json`));
    }
    packagePaths.push(...Object.values(layer.reportPaths || {}).map((entry) => path.resolve(clone, entry)));
    if (layer === gate) packagePaths.push(...actorPaths, ...reportPaths);
    for (const evidenceId of layer.evidenceIds || []) {
      const manifestPath = path.join(clone, "docs", "ai", "evidence", `${evidenceId}.json`);
      packagePaths.push(manifestPath);
      try {
        const evidence = parser.parseEvidenceManifest(manifestPath);
        packagePaths.push(path.resolve(clone, evidence.rawArtifact.path));
      } catch {}
    }
    if (layer.repair?.receiptPath) packagePaths.push(path.resolve(clone, layer.repair.receiptPath));
    if (layer.processJudge?.decisionPath) packagePaths.push(path.resolve(clone, layer.processJudge.decisionPath));
    const relativePaths = [...new Set(packagePaths.map((entry) => path.relative(clone, entry).replaceAll(path.sep, "/")))];
    if (relativePaths.some((entry) => !entry || entry.startsWith("../") || !/^docs\/ai\//.test(entry))) {
      failures.push(`${scope}: formal story-close package contains a non-control path`);
      return failures;
    }
    for (const relativePath of relativePaths) {
      const committed = committedUnchangedAtHead(clone, path.join(clone, relativePath));
      if (!committed.ok) failures.push(`${scope}: ${relativePath} ${committed.reason}`);
      const history = execute("git", ["log", "--format=%H", "--", relativePath], clone);
      const historyCommits = history.status === 0 ? history.stdout.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean) : [];
      if (historyCommits.length !== 1) failures.push(`${scope}: ${relativePath} changed after its immutable introduction`);
    }
    const deltaPaths = relativePaths.filter((entry) => !seenPaths.has(entry));
    if (!deltaPaths.length) {
      failures.push(`${scope}: formal story-close layer ${layer.gateId} introduces no new control evidence`);
      continue;
    }
    const introductionCommits = new Set();
    for (const relativePath of deltaPaths) {
      const added = execute("git", ["log", "--format=%H", "--diff-filter=A", "--", relativePath], clone);
      const commits = added.status === 0 ? added.stdout.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean) : [];
      if (commits.length !== 1) failures.push(`${scope}: ${relativePath} was not introduced exactly once`);
      else introductionCommits.add(commits[0]);
    }
    if (introductionCommits.size !== 1) {
      failures.push(`${scope}: formal story-close layer ${layer.gateId} files were not introduced in one commit`);
    } else {
      const [packageCommit] = [...introductionCommits];
      const changed = execute("git", ["diff-tree", "--root", "--no-commit-id", "--name-only", "-r", packageCommit, "--"], clone);
      const changedPaths = changed.status === 0 ? changed.stdout.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean).sort() : [];
      if (JSON.stringify(changedPaths) !== JSON.stringify([...deltaPaths].sort())) {
        failures.push(`${scope}: formal story-close layer ${layer.gateId} introduction commit is not exactly the bound control delta`);
      }
    }
    relativePaths.forEach((entry) => seenPaths.add(entry));
  }
  return failures;
}

function validateDurableLifecycleEvidence(clone, expectedContract, acceptedActors = expectedContract, options = {}) {
  const failures = [];
  const v3Contract = options.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3";
  const expectedRunId = options.runId || "";
  const expectedStoryInventory = options.storyInventory || [];
  if (v3Contract && !expectedRunId) failures.push("four-actor-v3 durable validation requires runId");
  if (v3Contract && !expectedStoryInventory.length) failures.push("four-actor-v3 durable validation requires frozen storyInventory");
  let parser;
  try { parser = installedStateParser(clone); }
  catch (error) { return { ok: false, actorCount: 0, gateCount: 0, failures: [error.message] }; }
  const actorDir = path.join(clone, "docs", "ai", "actors");
  const gateDir = path.join(clone, "docs", "ai", "gates");
  const actors = new Map();
  if (fs.existsSync(actorDir)) for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(actorDir).filter((name) => name.endsWith(".json"))) {
    try {
      const actor = parser.parseActorRecord(path.join(actorDir, entry));
      Object.defineProperty(actor, "_recordPath", { value: path.join(actorDir, entry), enumerable: false });
      if (actors.has(actor.actorInstanceId)) failures.push(`${entry}: duplicate actorInstanceId ${actor.actorInstanceId}`);
      actors.set(actor.actorInstanceId, actor);
    }
    catch (error) { failures.push(`${entry}: ${error.message}`); }
  }
  const gates = [];
  if (fs.existsSync(gateDir)) for (const entry of fs.readdirSync(gateDir).filter((name) => name.endsWith(".json"))) {
    try {
      const gate = parser.parseGateVerdict(path.join(gateDir, entry));
      Object.defineProperty(gate, "_recordPath", { value: path.join(gateDir, entry), enumerable: false });
      gates.push(gate);
    }
    catch (error) { failures.push(`${entry}: ${error.message}`); }
  }
  for (const expected of expectedContract) {
    const actor = actors.get(expected.taskName);
    if (!actor) { failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: typed actor record missing`); continue; }
    if (normalizedActorToken(actor.story) !== normalizedActorToken(expected.scope)) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: actor scope mismatch`);
    if (canonicalLifecyclePhase(actor.phase) !== canonicalLifecyclePhase(expected.control)) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: actor phase mismatch`);
    if (canonicalLifecyclePhase(actor.role) !== canonicalLifecyclePhase(expected.persona)) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: actor persona mismatch`);
    if (v3Contract && (actor.runId !== expectedRunId || actor.fullFlowContract !== "four-actor-v3")) {
      failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: actor run/contract binding mismatch`);
    }
    if (v3Contract && JSON.stringify(actor.storyInventory || []) !== JSON.stringify(expectedStoryInventory)) {
      failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: actor storyInventory does not match the frozen run inventory`);
    }
    const ancestor = execute("git", ["merge-base", "--is-ancestor", actor.inputCommit, "HEAD"], clone);
    if (ancestor.status !== 0) failures.push(`${expected.taskName}: inputCommit is not an ancestor of HEAD`);
  }
  if (v3Contract) {
    for (const scope of [...new Set(expectedContract.map((entry) => entry.scope).filter((entry) => entry !== "epic"))]) {
      const repairEntries = expectedContract.filter((entry) => entry.scope === scope
        && ["code-review", "patch-assurance"].includes(entry.control) && Number(entry.retryOrdinal || 0) > 0);
      for (const ordinal of [...new Set(repairEntries.map((entry) => Number(entry.retryOrdinal)))]) {
        const cycleActors = repairEntries.filter((entry) => entry.retryOrdinal === ordinal).map((entry) => actors.get(entry.taskName)).filter(Boolean);
        const inputTrees = new Set(cycleActors.map((actor) => actor.inputTree).filter(Boolean));
        if (cycleActors.some((actor) => !actor.inputTree) || inputTrees.size !== 1) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: repair cycle ${ordinal} reviewers do not bind one shared repaired input tree`);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  const scopes = [...new Set(expectedContract.map((entry) => entry.scope))];
  for (const scope of scopes) {
    if (v3Contract && scope !== "epic") {
      const storyPassGates = gates.filter((entry) => entry.verdict === "PASS"
        && normalizedActorToken(entry.scope) === normalizedActorToken(scope)
        && entry.runId === expectedRunId && entry.fullFlowContract === "four-actor-v3"
        && JSON.stringify(entry.storyInventory || []) === JSON.stringify(expectedStoryInventory)
        && entry.gateType === "deterministic-story-close-v3" && entry.decisionMode === "deterministic");
      if (storyPassGates.length !== 1) {
        failures.push(`${scope}: expected exactly one deterministic story-close PASS gate, observed ${storyPassGates.length}`);
        continue;
      }
      const [gate] = storyPassGates;
      const storyContract = (options.stories || []).find((entry) => normalizedActorToken(entry.id) === normalizedActorToken(scope));
      const frozenScopePaths = new Set([...(storyContract?.allowedPaths || []), ...(storyContract?.testPaths || [])]);
      if (!Array.isArray(gate.scopePaths) || !gate.scopePaths.length
        || gate.scopePaths.some((entry) => !frozenScopePaths.has(entry))) {
        failures.push(`${scope}: deterministic gate scopePaths escape the frozen production/test envelope`);
      }
      if (options.lifecycleIntegration && (!options.lifecycleIntegration.ok
        || !Number.isFinite(Date.parse(gate.createdAt || ""))
        || Date.parse(gate.createdAt) >= Date.parse(options.lifecycleIntegration.startedAt || ""))) {
        failures.push(`${scope}: story PASS gate was not durably complete before the frozen lifecycle integration command`);
      }
      requireCommittedUnchanged(failures, scope, "deterministic story-close gate", clone, gate._recordPath);
      const packageActorPaths = [];
      const requiredActorIds = ["atdd", "development", "code-review", "patch-assurance"].map((control) =>
        acceptedActors.find((entry) => entry.scope === scope && entry.control === control)?.taskName
      ).filter(Boolean);
      if (requiredActorIds.length !== 4) failures.push(`${scope}: deterministic close does not have four accepted required actors`);
      const recordedActorIds = new Set([
        ...(gate.actorInstanceIds || []),
        ...(gate.actors ? Object.values(gate.actors) : []),
        gate.atddActorId,
        gate.developmentActorId,
        gate.codeReviewActorId,
        gate.patchAssuranceActorId,
      ].filter(Boolean));
      for (const actorId of requiredActorIds) {
        if (!recordedActorIds.has(actorId)) failures.push(`${scope}: deterministic gate does not bind ${actorId}`);
        const actor = actors.get(actorId);
        if (actor) {
          requireCommittedUnchanged(failures, scope, `actor record ${actorId}`, clone, actor._recordPath);
          packageActorPaths.push(actor._recordPath);
        }
      }
      const acceptedCodeReviewId = acceptedActors.find((entry) => entry.scope === scope && entry.control === "code-review")?.taskName;
      const acceptedPatchAssuranceId = acceptedActors.find((entry) => entry.scope === scope && entry.control === "patch-assurance")?.taskName;
      const codeReviewActor = actors.get(acceptedCodeReviewId);
      const patchAssuranceActor = actors.get(acceptedPatchAssuranceId);
      if (codeReviewActor) {
        const scopePaths = new Set(gate.scopePaths || []);
        const changed = changedPathsFromCommit(clone, codeReviewActor.inputCommit);
        if (!changed || changed.some((entry) => scopePaths.has(entry) && !/^(?:tests?|spec)(?:\/|$)/i.test(entry))) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: Code Review predates a non-test application repair and requires delta review`);
        }
      }
      if (patchAssuranceActor) {
        const scopePaths = new Set(gate.scopePaths || []);
        const changed = changedPathsFromCommit(clone, patchAssuranceActor.inputCommit);
        if (!changed || changed.some((entry) => scopePaths.has(entry))) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: Patch Assurance does not bind the final application/test tree`);
        }
      }
      const boundReports = {};
      const packageReportPaths = [];
      for (const [role, actorId, expectedPhase] of [
        ["codeReview", acceptedCodeReviewId, "codereview"],
        ["patchAssurance", acceptedPatchAssuranceId, "patchassurance"],
      ]) {
        const actor = actors.get(actorId);
        const reportPathValue = gate.reportPaths?.[role];
        const reportHash = gate.reportHashes?.[role];
        if (!actor || !reportPathValue) continue;
        const reportPath = path.resolve(clone, reportPathValue);
        packageReportPaths.push(reportPath);
        requireCommittedUnchanged(failures, scope, `${role} report`, clone, reportPath);
        try {
          const report = parser.parseReviewReport(reportPath);
          boundReports[role] = report;
          if (actor.producedArtifactPath !== reportPathValue || actor.producedArtifactHash !== reportHash
            || sha256File(reportPath) !== reportHash) {
            failures.push(`${scope}: ${role} report path/hash does not bind its actor and gate`);
          }
          if (report.actorInstanceId !== actorId || normalizedActorToken(report.story) !== normalizedActorToken(scope)
            || canonicalLifecyclePhase(report.phase) !== expectedPhase
            || report.inputCommit !== actor.inputCommit || report.inputTree !== actor.inputTree
            || report.runId !== expectedRunId || report.fullFlowContract !== "four-actor-v3") {
            failures.push(`${scope}: ${role} report identity/scope/input binding mismatch`);
          }
          const captured = (options.reviewerCompletions || []).find((entry) => entry.taskName === actorId);
          if (!captured || captured.reportPath !== reportPathValue || captured.reportSha256 !== reportHash
            || captured.inputTree !== actor.inputTree || Buffer.from(captured.reportBase64 || "", "base64").toString("utf8") !== fs.readFileSync(reportPath, "utf8")) {
            failures.push(`${scope}: ${role} gate/report does not bind the reviewer child-completion blob and input tree`);
          }
          if (report.verdict !== "PASS" || report.findings.some((finding) => finding.status === "OPEN")) {
            failures.push(`${scope}: ${role} report has unresolved findings or non-PASS verdict`);
          }
        } catch (error) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: ${role} report: ${error.message}`);
        }
      }
      if (boundReports.codeReview && boundReports.patchAssurance) {
        const findings = new Map();
        for (const report of [boundReports.codeReview, boundReports.patchAssurance]) {
          for (const finding of report.findings) findings.set(finding.id, finding);
        }
        const dispositions = [...findings.values()].map((finding) => {
          const disposition = { id: finding.id, severity: finding.severity, status: finding.status };
          if (finding.reason) disposition.reason = finding.reason;
          if (finding.approvalId) disposition.approvalId = finding.approvalId;
          return disposition;
        }).sort((left, right) => left.id.localeCompare(right.id));
        const unresolved = dispositions.filter((finding) => finding.status === "OPEN")
          .map(({ severity, id }) => ({ severity, id }));
        if (JSON.stringify(dispositions) !== JSON.stringify(gate.findingDispositions || [])) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: gate finding dispositions do not match bound review reports`);
        }
        if (JSON.stringify(unresolved) !== JSON.stringify(gate.unresolvedFindings || [])) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: gate unresolved findings do not match bound review reports`);
        }
      }
      const conditionalJudge = acceptedActors.find((entry) => entry.scope === scope && entry.control === "process-judge");
      if (conditionalJudge) {
        const boundJudge = gate.processJudge?.actorId;
        const trigger = gate.processJudge?.trigger;
        if (boundJudge !== conditionalJudge.taskName || !["ambiguity", "waiver", "evidence-conflict", "gate-anomaly"].includes(trigger)) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: conditional Process Judge is not bound to an allowed deterministic-gate trigger`);
        }
        try {
          const decisionPath = path.resolve(clone, gate.processJudge?.decisionPath || "");
          const decision = parser.parseProcessJudgeDecision(decisionPath);
          requireCommittedUnchanged(failures, scope, "Process Judge decision", clone, decisionPath);
          if (sha256File(decisionPath) !== gate.processJudge.decisionSha256
            || decision.runId !== expectedRunId || decision.fullFlowContract !== "four-actor-v3"
            || normalizedActorToken(decision.story) !== normalizedActorToken(scope)
            || decision.actorId !== conditionalJudge.taskName || decision.trigger !== trigger
            || decision.gateId !== gate.gateId || decision.verdict !== gate.processJudge.verdict
            || JSON.stringify([...decision.evidenceIds].sort()) !== JSON.stringify([...(gate.evidenceIds || [])].sort())) {
            failures.push(`${scope}: conditional Process Judge decision binding mismatch`);
          }
        } catch (error) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: conditional Process Judge decision: ${error.message}`);
        }
      }
      if (gate.reviewCycle > 0) {
        try {
          const receiptPath = path.resolve(clone, gate.repair?.receiptPath || "");
          const receipt = parser.parseDeveloperRepair(receiptPath);
          requireCommittedUnchanged(failures, scope, "Developer repair receipt", clone, receiptPath);
          const reactivation = (options.developerReactivations || []).find((entry) => entry.scope === scope
            && entry.repairCycle === gate.reviewCycle);
          const priorGate = gates.find((entry) => entry.gateId === gate.repair.priorGateId);
          if (sha256File(receiptPath) !== gate.repair.receiptSha256
            || receipt.runId !== expectedRunId || receipt.fullFlowContract !== "four-actor-v3"
            || normalizedActorToken(receipt.story) !== normalizedActorToken(scope)
            || receipt.cycle !== gate.reviewCycle || receipt.priorGateId !== gate.repair.priorGateId
            || receipt.developerActorId !== gate.actors.development || receipt.developerActorId !== gate.repair.developerActorId
            || receipt.developerSessionId !== reactivation?.developerSessionId
            || gate.repair.receiptPath !== reactivation?.repairReceiptPath
            || gate.repair.receiptSha256 !== reactivation?.repairReceiptSha256
            || receipt.postTree !== gate.applicationTree
            || !priorGate || priorGate.runId !== expectedRunId || priorGate.verdict !== "REVISE") {
            failures.push(`${scope}: Developer repair receipt binding mismatch`);
          }
        } catch (error) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: Developer repair receipt: ${error.message}`);
        }
      }
      failures.push(...validateGateEvidence(scope, gate, clone, parser, actors));
      failures.push(...validateFormalStoryClosePackage(scope, gate, clone, packageActorPaths, packageReportPaths, parser, gates));
      continue;
    }
    const judge = acceptedActors.find((entry) => entry.scope === scope && entry.control === "process-judge");
    const matchingEpicGates = gates.filter((entry) => entry.verdict === "PASS"
      && normalizedActorToken(entry.scope) === normalizedActorToken(scope)
      && entry.decidedBy === judge?.taskName
      && (!v3Contract || (entry.runId === expectedRunId && entry.fullFlowContract === "four-actor-v3"
        && JSON.stringify(entry.storyInventory || []) === JSON.stringify(expectedStoryInventory))));
    if (v3Contract && scope === "epic" && matchingEpicGates.length !== 1) {
      failures.push(`epic: expected exactly one run-bound PASS gate, observed ${matchingEpicGates.length}`);
      continue;
    }
    const gate = matchingEpicGates[0];
    if (!gate) { failures.push(`${scope}: typed PASS gate from required Process Judge missing`); continue; }
    failures.push(...validateGateEvidence(scope, gate, clone, parser, actors));
  }
  return { ok: failures.length === 0, actorCount: actors.size, gateCount: gates.length, failures };
}

function validateGateEvidence(scope, gate, clone, parser, actors) {
  const failures = [];
  if (!Array.isArray(gate.evidenceIds) || !gate.evidenceIds.length) failures.push(`${scope}: PASS gate has no evidenceIds`);
  if (gate.gateType === "deterministic-story-close-v3"
    && (!gate.evidenceIds?.includes(gate.redEvidenceId) || !gate.evidenceIds?.includes(gate.greenEvidenceId))) {
    failures.push(`${scope}: deterministic gate evidenceIds must directly include redEvidenceId and greenEvidenceId`);
  }
  if (execute("git", ["merge-base", "--is-ancestor", gate.repositoryCommit, "HEAD"], clone).status !== 0) {
    failures.push(`${scope}: gate repositoryCommit is not an ancestor of HEAD`);
  }
  for (const evidenceId of gate.evidenceIds || []) {
    const evidencePath = path.join(clone, "docs", "ai", "evidence", `${evidenceId}.json`);
    try {
      const evidence = parser.parseEvidenceManifest(evidencePath);
      if (gate.gateType === "deterministic-story-close-v3") {
        requireCommittedUnchanged(failures, scope, `evidence manifest ${evidenceId}`, clone, evidencePath);
        if (!Array.isArray(evidence.dirtyApplicationPathsBefore) || evidence.dirtyApplicationPathsBefore.length
          || !Array.isArray(evidence.dirtyApplicationPathsAfter) || evidence.dirtyApplicationPathsAfter.length) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: evidence ${evidenceId} must start and finish with no dirty application paths`);
        }
        const recordedTree = execute("git", ["rev-parse", `${evidence.repositoryCommit}^{tree}`], clone);
        if (!evidence.repositoryTree || recordedTree.status !== 0 || recordedTree.stdout.trim() !== evidence.repositoryTree) {
          failures.push(`${scope}: evidence ${evidenceId} repository tree binding is invalid`);
        }
      }
      if (evidence.evidenceId !== evidenceId) failures.push(`${scope}: evidence filename/id mismatch for ${evidenceId}`);
      const expectedRed = gate.redEvidenceId === evidenceId;
      if (expectedRed ? evidence.exitCode === 0 : evidence.exitCode !== 0) {
        failures.push(`${scope}: evidence ${evidenceId} has the wrong ${expectedRed ? "red" : "green"} exit status`);
      }
      if (gate.gateType === "deterministic-story-close-v3" && expectedRed
        && !committedRedIsTestOnly(clone, evidence.repositoryCommit)) {
        failures.push(`${scope}: red evidence ${evidenceId} is not bound to a committed test-only tree`);
      }
      if (normalizedActorToken(evidence.story) !== normalizedActorToken(scope)) failures.push(`${scope}: evidence ${evidenceId} scope mismatch`);
      if (!actors.has(evidence.actorInstanceId)) failures.push(`${scope}: evidence ${evidenceId} actor is missing`);
      else if (normalizedActorToken(actors.get(evidence.actorInstanceId).story) !== normalizedActorToken(scope)) failures.push(`${scope}: evidence ${evidenceId} actor scope mismatch`);
      if (execute("git", ["merge-base", "--is-ancestor", evidence.repositoryCommit, "HEAD"], clone).status !== 0) failures.push(`${scope}: evidence ${evidenceId} repositoryCommit is not an ancestor of HEAD`);
      const rawArtifact = path.resolve(clone, evidence.rawArtifact.path);
      const relative = path.relative(clone, rawArtifact);
      if (!relative || relative.startsWith("..") || path.isAbsolute(relative)) failures.push(`${scope}: evidence ${evidenceId} artifact escapes clone`);
      else if (!fs.existsSync(rawArtifact)) failures.push(`${scope}: evidence ${evidenceId} artifact missing`);
      else if (path.relative(fs.realpathSync(clone), fs.realpathSync(rawArtifact)).startsWith("..") || sha256File(rawArtifact) !== evidence.rawArtifact.sha256) failures.push(`${scope}: evidence ${evidenceId} artifact/hash mismatch`);
      else if (gate.gateType === "deterministic-story-close-v3") {
        requireCommittedUnchanged(failures, scope, `raw artifact ${evidenceId}`, clone, rawArtifact);
      }
    } catch (error) { failures.push(`${scope}: evidence ${evidenceId}: ${error.message}`); }
  }
  return failures;
}

function runnerSourceSha256() {
  const sourcePaths = [
    "scripts/acef-execution-assurance-experiment",
    "scripts/acef-execution-assurance-actor",
    "scripts/lib/acef-execution-assurance-experiment.js",
    "scripts/lib/acef-state-parser.js",
    "scripts/lib/acef-execution-policy.js",
    "scripts/lib/acef-empirical.js",
    "scripts/acef-empirical-validation",
  ];
  return sha256(sourcePaths.map((entry) => `${entry}\0${fs.readFileSync(path.join(root, entry), "utf8")}\0`).join(""));
}

function runCollaborationCanary(manifest) {
  const runtime = resolvePinnedClient(manifest.pilotRuntime);
  const directory = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), "acef-pilot-collaboration-canary-"));
  const taskName = "acef_pilot_canary";
  try {
    must("git", ["init", "-q"], directory);
    must("git", ["config", "user.email", "acef-canary@example.invalid"], directory);
    must("git", ["config", "user.name", "ACEF Canary"], directory);
    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(directory, "README.md"), "ACEF collaboration canary\n");
    must("git", ["add", "README.md"], directory);
    must("git", ["commit", "-qm", "canary"], directory);
    const prompt = `Call collaboration.spawn_agent exactly once with task_name=${taskName}, fork_turns=none, and ask it to reply exactly ACTOR_RESULT=PASS. Then call wait_agent until that exact child returns a final answer. Reply RESULT=PASS only after the real child result; otherwise RESULT=FAIL.`;
    const result = execute(runtime.clientPath, [
      "exec", "--json", "--ignore-user-config",
      "--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox", "--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust",
      "--model", manifest.pilotRuntime.model,
      "--config", `model_reasoning_effort=${JSON.stringify(manifest.pilotRuntime.reasoningEffort)}`,
      "-C", directory,
      prompt,
    ], directory, { timeout: 180000 });
    let threadId = null;
    for (const line of result.stdout.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)) {
      try { const event = JSON.parse(line); if (event.type === "thread.started") threadId = event.thread_id; } catch {}
    }
    const expected = [{ scope: "canary", control: "spawn", persona: "probe", retryable: false, taskName }];
    const rawPath = path.join(directory, "canary-raw.jsonl");
    fs.writeFileSync(rawPath, result.stdout);
    const evidence = threadId
      ? loadCollaborationEvidence(rawPath, expected, {
        cwd: directory,
        clientVersion: runtime.observedClientVersion.replace(/^codex-cli\s+/, ""),
      })
      : { ok: false, threadId, failures: ["canary session transcript not found"], dispatches: [] };
    const ok = result.status === 0 && evidence.ok;
    return {
      ok,
      checkedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
      clientPath: runtime.clientPath,
      clientBinarySha256: runtime.clientBinarySha256,
      clientVersion: runtime.observedClientVersion,
      model: manifest.pilotRuntime.model,
      reasoningEffort: manifest.pilotRuntime.reasoningEffort,
      threadId,
      exitCode: result.status,
      expectedActorCount: evidence.expectedActorCount || 1,
      observedActorCount: evidence.observedActorCount || 0,
      receiverThreadIds: (evidence.dispatches || []).map((entry) => entry.receiverThreadId).filter(Boolean),
      sessionSha256: evidence.sessionSha256 || null,
      failures: [...(evidence.failures || []), ...(result.status === 0 ? [] : [`client exited ${result.status}`])],
    };
  } finally {
    fs.rmSync(directory, { recursive: true, force: true });
  }
}

function resolvePinnedClient(runtime) {
  const discovered = path.isAbsolute(runtime.client)
    ? runtime.client
    : must("which", [runtime.client], root);
  const clientPath = fs.realpathSync(discovered);
  const observedClientVersion = must(clientPath, ["--version"], root);
  if (observedClientVersion !== runtime.clientVersion) {
    throw new Error(`pilot client version mismatch: observed ${observedClientVersion}, expected ${runtime.clientVersion}`);
  }
  return {
    clientPath,
    clientBinarySha256: sha256File(clientPath),
    observedClientVersion,
  };
}

function pilotAgentRequest(attempt, resolved, clone, manifest, rawPath, receiptPath, clientRuntime) {
  const runtime = manifest.pilotRuntime;
  const args = [
    "exec", "--json", "--ignore-user-config",
    "--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox", "--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust",
    "--model", runtime.model,
    "--config", `model_reasoning_effort=${JSON.stringify(runtime.reasoningEffort)}`,
    "-C", clone,
  ];
  if (attempt.treatment === "repo-native") args.push("--ignore-rules");
  args.push(resolved.kind === "epic" ? epicPilotPrompt(attempt, resolved, manifest) : pilotPrompt(attempt, resolved));
  return {
    command: clientRuntime.clientPath,
    args,
    cwd: clone,
    stdoutPath: rawPath,
    stderrPath: `${rawPath}.stderr`,
    receiptPath,
    timeoutMs: attempt.activeTimeCapMinutes * 60 * 1000,
    ...(attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3" ? {
      livePolicy: {
        schema: "acef.execution-assurance-live-policy.v1",
        allowedFollowupTargets: resolved.task.stories.map((story) =>
          `/root/acef_${normalizedActorToken(story.id)}_development`),
      },
    } : {}),
  };
}

function launchPilotAgent(requestPath, cwd) {
  const actorScript = path.join(root, "scripts", "acef-execution-assurance-actor");
  const child = cp.spawn(process.execPath, [actorScript, requestPath], {
    cwd,
    detached: true,
    stdio: "ignore",
  });
  child.unref();
  return child.pid;
}

function waitForFile(filePath, timeoutMs) {
  const deadline = Date.now() + timeoutMs;
  const signal = new Int32Array(new SharedArrayBuffer(4));
  while (Date.now() < deadline) {
    if (fs.existsSync(filePath)) return true;
    Atomics.wait(signal, 0, 0, 1000);
  }
  return fs.existsSync(filePath);
}

function processAlive(pid) {
  if (!Number.isInteger(pid)) return false;
  try { process.kill(pid, 0); return true; } catch { return false; }
}

function processGroupAlive(pid) {
  if (!Number.isInteger(pid)) return false;
  try { process.kill(-pid, 0); return true; } catch { return false; }
}

function waitForReceiptOrExit(receiptPath, supervisorPid, timeoutMs) {
  const deadline = Date.now() + timeoutMs;
  const signal = new Int32Array(new SharedArrayBuffer(4));
  while (Date.now() < deadline) {
    if (fs.existsSync(receiptPath)) return "receipt";
    if (!processAlive(supervisorPid)) return "exited";
    Atomics.wait(signal, 0, 0, 1000);
  }
  return fs.existsSync(receiptPath) ? "receipt" : "timeout";
}

function ensureActorRequestLocked(checkpoint, config, graceChecked = false) {
  if (fs.existsSync(config.receiptPath)) {
    const receipt = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(config.receiptPath, "utf8"));
    if (receipt.requestSha256 !== config.requestSha256 || receipt.launchNonce !== config.launchNonce) {
      throw new Error(`${checkpoint.attemptRunId} ${config.label} receipt binding mismatch`);
    }
    return checkpoint;
  }
  if (fs.existsSync(config.startPath)) {
    const started = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(config.startPath, "utf8"));
    if (started.requestSha256 !== config.requestSha256 || started.launchNonce !== config.launchNonce) {
      throw new Error(`${checkpoint.attemptRunId} ${config.label} start binding mismatch`);
    }
    if (processAlive(started.supervisorPid)) {
      const waitResult = waitForReceiptOrExit(config.receiptPath, started.supervisorPid, config.timeoutMs + 60000);
      if (waitResult === "receipt") return ensureActorRequestLocked(checkpoint, config, true);
      if (waitResult === "timeout") {
        throw new Error(`${checkpoint.attemptRunId} ${config.label} is still running or has no receipt`);
      }
    }
    if (processGroupAlive(started.processGroupPid)) {
      try { process.kill(-started.processGroupPid, "SIGKILL"); } catch (error) {
        if (error.code !== "ESRCH") throw error;
      }
      const signal = new Int32Array(new SharedArrayBuffer(4));
      for (let index = 0; index < 40 && processGroupAlive(started.processGroupPid); index += 1) Atomics.wait(signal, 0, 0, 50);
      if (processGroupAlive(started.processGroupPid)) throw new Error(`${checkpoint.attemptRunId} orphaned ${config.label} group did not quiesce`);
    }
    if (!config.relaunchAfterStartedExit) {
      throw new Error(`${checkpoint.attemptRunId} ${config.label} started but exited without a receipt; side effects are indeterminate and the attempt must be adjudicated, not replayed`);
    }
    fs.renameSync(config.startPath, `${config.startPath}.orphaned-${Date.now()}`);
  } else if (!graceChecked) {
    waitForFile(config.startPath, 2000);
    return ensureActorRequestLocked(checkpoint, config, true);
  }
  const supervisorPid = launchPilotAgent(config.requestPath, checkpoint.clone);
  const launched = { ...checkpoint, status: config.status, [config.pidField]: supervisorPid };
  writeJsonAtomic(checkpoint.checkpointPath, launched);
  if (!waitForFile(config.receiptPath, config.timeoutMs + 60000)) {
    throw new Error(`${checkpoint.attemptRunId} ${config.label} has no receipt; retry later`);
  }
  return ensureActorRequestLocked(launched, config, true);
}

function ensureActorRequest(checkpoint, config, graceChecked = false) {
  if (fs.existsSync(config.receiptPath)) return ensureActorRequestLocked(checkpoint, config, graceChecked);
  const pilotWorkspace = path.dirname(path.dirname(checkpoint.checkpointPath));
  const claim = acquireFinalizationClaim(
    checkpoint.checkpointPath,
    `${checkpoint.attemptRunId}-${config.label}-launch`,
    path.join(pilotWorkspace, "launch-locks"),
  );
  try {
    return ensureActorRequestLocked(checkpoint, config, graceChecked);
  } finally {
    claim.release();
  }
}

function changedPaths(repo, baseRef) {
  const diff = must("git", ["diff", "--name-only", `${baseRef}..HEAD`], repo).split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean);
  const status = execute("git", ["status", "--porcelain=v1", "--untracked-files=all"], repo);
  if (status.status !== 0) throw new Error(`git status failed: ${status.stderr || status.stdout}`);
  const working = status.stdout.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean).map((line) => line.slice(3));
  return [...new Set([...diff, ...working])].sort();
}

function findPilotAttempt(manifest, attemptId) {
  const attempt = buildPilotPlan(manifest).find((entry) => entry.id === attemptId);
  if (!attempt) throw new Error(`pilot attempt not preregistered: ${attemptId}`);
  return attempt;
}

function pilotCheckpointPath(opts, attemptRunId) {
  return path.join(opts.pilotWorkspace, "checkpoints", `${attemptRunId}.json`);
}

function resolvedTaskSha256(resolved) {
  const setup = resolved.kind === "epic"
    ? resolved.task.stories.flatMap((story) => story.setup || [])
    : (resolved.task.setup || []);
  const fixtureHashes = setup.filter((operation) => operation.type === "copy-fixture").map((operation) => ({
    fixture: operation.fixture,
    sha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(path.join(resolved.fixtureRoot, operation.fixture))),
  }));
  const referencePatchHashes = (resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.stories : [resolved.task])
    .filter((story) => story.referencePatch)
    .map((story) => ({
      storyId: story.id || resolved.taskId,
      referencePatch: story.referencePatch,
      sha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(storyReferencePatchPath(resolved, story))),
    }));
  return sha256(JSON.stringify({
    taskId: resolved.taskId,
    selector: resolved.selector,
    kind: resolved.kind,
    sourceManifestPath: resolved.sourceManifestPath,
    fixtureRoot: resolved.fixtureRoot,
    repo: resolved.repo,
    stack: resolved.stack,
    source: resolved.source,
    commit: resolved.commit,
    setupDirs: resolved.setupDirs,
    setupFiles: resolved.setupFiles,
    sourceManifestSha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(resolved.sourceManifestPath)),
    fixtureHashes,
    referencePatchHashes,
    task: resolved.task,
  }));
}

function frozenProductContract(resolved) {
  const stories = resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.stories : [resolved.task];
  const contract = {
    schema: "acef.execution-assurance-product-contract.v1",
    taskId: resolved.taskId,
    kind: resolved.kind,
    stories: stories.map((story) => ({
      id: story.id || resolved.taskId,
      prompt: story.prompt,
      acceptanceCriteria: story.acceptanceCriteria || story.ac || [],
      dependsOn: story.dependsOn || [],
      allowedPaths: story.allowedPaths || [],
      testPaths: story.testPaths || [],
      atddConstraints: story.atddConstraints || [],
    })),
  };
  return { contract, sha256: sha256(JSON.stringify(contract)) };
}

function withheldOracleSha256(resolved) {
  const stories = resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.stories : [resolved.task];
  return sha256(JSON.stringify({
    stories: stories.map((story) => ({ id: story.id || resolved.taskId, setup: story.setup || [], verify: story.verify || [], expected: story.expected || [] })),
    integration: resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.integration : null,
  }));
}

function catalogTaskBindings(manifest, manifestPath) {
  return Object.keys(manifest.taskCatalog || {}).sort().map((taskId) => {
    const resolved = resolveCatalogTask(manifest, manifestPath, taskId);
    return { taskId, resolvedTaskSha256: resolvedTaskSha256(resolved) };
  });
}

function reconcileFinalizedCheckpoint(checkpoint, row) {
  writeJsonAtomic(checkpoint.checkpointPath, {
    ...checkpoint,
    status: "finalized",
    finalizedAt: row.finishedAt,
    result: row.result,
    reconciledFromResult: true,
  });
}

function validateCheckpointInputs(opts, checkpoint, resolved, receipt, manifest) {
  const clientRuntime = resolvePinnedClient(manifest.pilotRuntime);
  const checks = [
    [path.resolve(opts.manifest) === checkpoint.manifestPath, "manifest path drift"],
    [sha256(fs.readFileSync(opts.manifest, "utf8")) === checkpoint.manifestSha256, "manifest content drift"],
    [resolvedTaskSha256(resolved) === checkpoint.resolvedTaskSha256, "resolved task/oracle drift"],
    [path.resolve(opts.pilotResults) === checkpoint.pilotResultsPath, "pilot results destination drift"],
    [must("git", ["rev-parse", "HEAD"], root) === checkpoint.runnerCommit, "runner commit drift"],
    [sha256(must("git", ["status", "--porcelain"], root)) === checkpoint.runnerWorktreeSha256, "runner worktree drift"],
    [sha256(fs.readFileSync(checkpoint.requestPath, "utf8")) === checkpoint.requestSha256, "actor request drift"],
    [receipt.requestPath === checkpoint.requestPath, "receipt request path mismatch"],
    [receipt.requestSha256 === checkpoint.requestSha256, "receipt request hash mismatch"],
    [receipt.launchNonce === checkpoint.actorLaunchNonce, "receipt launch nonce mismatch"],
    [clientRuntime.clientPath === checkpoint.clientPath, "pilot client path drift"],
    [clientRuntime.clientBinarySha256 === checkpoint.clientBinarySha256, "pilot client binary drift"],
    [clientRuntime.observedClientVersion === checkpoint.observedClientVersion, "pilot client version drift"],
  ];
  const failed = checks.filter(([ok]) => !ok).map(([, message]) => message);
  if (failed.length) throw new Error(`${checkpoint.attemptRunId} checkpoint input validation failed: ${failed.join("; ")}`);
}

function evaluateTreatmentState(clone, attempt, frozenExpectedStories = [], expectedRunId = "") {
  if (attempt.treatment === "repo-native") return { ok: true, expected: "repo-native", observed: null, failures: [] };
  const activeRunPath = path.join(clone, "docs", "ai", "ACEF_ACTIVE_RUN.json");
  if (!fs.existsSync(activeRunPath)) {
    return { ok: false, expected: attempt.treatment, observed: null, failures: ["missing ACEF_ACTIVE_RUN.json"] };
  }
  let observed;
  const failures = [];
  try {
    observed = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(activeRunPath, "utf8"));
    installedStateParser(clone).parseActiveRun(activeRunPath);
  } catch (error) {
    return { ok: false, expected: attempt.treatment, observed: null, failures: [`invalid typed active run: ${error.message}`] };
  }
  if (attempt.treatment === "legacy") {
    if (observed.lane !== "full-bmad") failures.push(`legacy lane is ${observed.lane || "missing"}, expected full-bmad`);
    if (observed.workflowId || observed.assuranceProfile) failures.push("legacy state invented candidate execution/assurance axes");
  } else {
    if (observed.workflowId !== attempt.workflowId) failures.push(`candidate workflowId is ${observed.workflowId || "missing"}`);
    if (observed.assuranceProfile !== attempt.assuranceProfile) failures.push(`candidate assuranceProfile is ${observed.assuranceProfile || "missing"}`);
    if (attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3" && observed.fullFlowContract !== "four-actor-v3") {
      failures.push(`candidate fullFlowContract is ${observed.fullFlowContract || "missing"}`);
    }
    if (attempt.runtimeContract && observed.runtimeContract !== attempt.runtimeContract) {
      failures.push(`candidate runtimeContract is ${observed.runtimeContract || "missing"}`);
    }
    if (attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3"
      && JSON.stringify(observed.expectedStories || []) !== JSON.stringify(frozenExpectedStories)) {
      failures.push(`candidate expectedStories inventory does not match frozen task catalog`);
    }
    if (attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3" && expectedRunId && observed.runId !== expectedRunId) {
      failures.push(`candidate runId is ${observed.runId || "missing"}, expected ${expectedRunId}`);
    }
  }
  if (observed.status !== "complete") failures.push(`active run status is ${observed.status || "missing"}, expected complete`);
  return {
    ok: failures.length === 0,
    expected: attempt.treatment === "legacy" ? { lane: "full-bmad" }
      : { workflowId: attempt.workflowId, assuranceProfile: attempt.assuranceProfile, runtimeContract: attempt.runtimeContract || null },
    observed,
    observedSha256: sha256(JSON.stringify(observed)),
    failures,
  };
}

function frozenCommandText(argv) {
  return argv.map((value) => /^[A-Za-z0-9_./:@%+=,-]+$/.test(value)
    ? value : `'${value.replaceAll("'", `'\\''`)}'`).join(" ");
}

function validateFrozenDiscoveryContracts(clone, resolved, attempt) {
  if (attempt.runtimeContract !== "capsule-supervisor-v1") {
    return { ok: true, applicable: false, stories: [], failures: [] };
  }
  const failures = [];
  const results = [];
  const stories = resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.stories : [resolved.task];
  const gateDir = path.join(clone, "docs", "ai", "gates");
  const gates = fs.existsSync(gateDir) ? fs.readdirSync(gateDir).filter((name) => name.endsWith(".json")).map((name) => {
    try { return JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(gateDir, name), "utf8")); } catch { return null; }
  }).filter(Boolean) : [];
  for (const story of stories) {
    const discovery = story.discovery;
    const storyFailures = [];
    if (!discovery || !Array.isArray(discovery.argv) || !discovery.argv.length
      || !Array.isArray(discovery.expectedTests) || !discovery.expectedTests.length) {
      storyFailures.push("frozen discovery contract is missing");
    }
    const passGates = gates.filter((gate) => gate.gateType === "deterministic-story-close-v3"
      && gate.verdict === "PASS" && normalizedActorToken(gate.scope) === normalizedActorToken(story.id))
      .sort((left, right) => Number(right.reviewCycle || 0) - Number(left.reviewCycle || 0));
    const gate = passGates[0] || null;
    let evidence = null;
    if (!gate?.greenEvidenceId) {
      storyFailures.push("terminal PASS gate or greenEvidenceId is missing");
    } else {
      const evidencePath = path.join(clone, "docs", "ai", "evidence", `${gate.greenEvidenceId}.json`);
      try { evidence = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(evidencePath, "utf8")); }
      catch { storyFailures.push(`green evidence ${gate.greenEvidenceId} is missing or invalid`); }
    }
    if (evidence && discovery) {
      const expectedRunner = frozenCommandText(story.verify || []);
      const expectedDiscovery = frozenCommandText(discovery.argv);
      if (evidence.command !== expectedRunner) storyFailures.push("green runner command differs from the frozen focused argv");
      if (evidence.discovery?.command !== expectedDiscovery) storyFailures.push("discovery command differs from the frozen argv");
      if (JSON.stringify(evidence.discovery?.expectedTests || []) !== JSON.stringify(discovery.expectedTests)) {
        storyFailures.push("expected discovery identities differ from the frozen ordered list");
      }
      const discovered = new Set(evidence.discovery?.discoveredTests || []);
      if (discovery.expectedTests.some((identity) => !discovered.has(identity))) {
        storyFailures.push("one or more frozen test identities were not discovered");
      }
    }
    failures.push(...storyFailures.map((message) => `${story.id}: ${message}`));
    results.push({ story: story.id, gateId: gate?.gateId || null, evidenceId: gate?.greenEvidenceId || null, ok: storyFailures.length === 0, failures: storyFailures });
  }
  return { ok: failures.length === 0, applicable: true, stories: results, failures };
}

function latestPilotCheckpoint(opts, attemptId) {
  const directory = path.join(opts.pilotWorkspace, "checkpoints");
  if (!fs.existsSync(directory)) throw new Error(`no durable checkpoint exists for ${attemptId}`);
  const checkpoints = fs.readdirSync(directory).filter((entry) => entry.endsWith(".json"))
    .map((entry) => JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(directory, entry), "utf8")))
    .filter((entry) => entry.attemptId === attemptId)
    .sort((left, right) => Number(right.attemptOrdinal) - Number(left.attemptOrdinal));
  if (!checkpoints.length) throw new Error(`no durable checkpoint exists for ${attemptId}`);
  return checkpoints[0];
}

function ensureVerification(checkpoint, verificationContract) {
  const verificationCommandSha256 = sha256(JSON.stringify(verificationContract.verify));
  if (checkpoint.verificationCommandSha256 && checkpoint.verificationCommandSha256 !== verificationCommandSha256) {
    throw new Error(`${checkpoint.attemptRunId} verification command drift`);
  }
  if (checkpoint.verificationReceiptPath && fs.existsSync(checkpoint.verificationReceiptPath)) {
    const receipt = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(checkpoint.verificationReceiptPath, "utf8"));
    if (receipt.requestSha256 !== checkpoint.verificationRequestSha256
      || receipt.launchNonce !== checkpoint.verificationLaunchNonce) {
      throw new Error(`${checkpoint.attemptRunId} verification receipt hash mismatch`);
    }
    return { checkpoint, verification: { status: receipt.status, signal: receipt.signal } };
  }
  if (checkpoint.verificationStarted) {
    const resumed = ensureActorRequest(checkpoint, {
      label: "verification",
      requestPath: checkpoint.verificationRequestPath,
      receiptPath: checkpoint.verificationReceiptPath,
      startPath: checkpoint.verificationStartPath,
      requestSha256: checkpoint.verificationRequestSha256,
      launchNonce: checkpoint.verificationLaunchNonce,
      timeoutMs: checkpoint.verificationTimeoutMs,
      status: "verifying",
      pidField: "verificationPid",
      relaunchAfterStartedExit: true,
    });
    return ensureVerification(resumed, verificationContract);
  }
  const pilotWorkspace = path.dirname(path.dirname(checkpoint.checkpointPath));
  const base = path.join(pilotWorkspace, "verification", checkpoint.attemptRunId);
  const requestPath = `${base}.request.json`;
  const receiptPath = `${base}.receipt.json`;
  const request = {
    command: verificationContract.verify[0],
    args: verificationContract.verify.slice(1),
    cwd: checkpoint.clone,
    stdoutPath: `${base}.stdout`,
    stderrPath: `${base}.stderr`,
    receiptPath,
    startPath: `${base}.started.json`,
    launchNonce: `${checkpoint.attemptRunId}:verification:v1`,
    timeoutMs: 1200000,
  };
  writeJsonAtomic(requestPath, request);
  let verifyingCheckpoint = {
    ...checkpoint,
    status: "verifying",
    verificationStarted: true,
    verificationTimeoutMs: request.timeoutMs,
    verificationCommandSha256,
    verificationRequestPath: requestPath,
    verificationRequestSha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(requestPath, "utf8")),
    verificationReceiptPath: receiptPath,
    verificationStartPath: request.startPath,
    verificationLaunchNonce: request.launchNonce,
  };
  writeJsonAtomic(checkpoint.checkpointPath, verifyingCheckpoint);
  return ensureVerification(verifyingCheckpoint, verificationContract);
}

function writeArtifactOnlyJudgePacket(opts, payload) {
  const packetPath = path.join(opts.pilotWorkspace, "judge-packets", `${payload.attemptRunId}.json`);
  const packet = {
    schema: "acef.execution-assurance-judge-packet.v1",
    experimentId: payload.experimentId,
    attemptId: payload.attemptId,
    attemptRunId: payload.attemptRunId,
    attemptOrdinal: payload.attemptOrdinal,
    taskId: payload.taskId,
    storyInventory: payload.storyInventory,
    project: payload.project,
    projectCommit: payload.projectCommit,
    productContract: payload.productContract,
    productContractSha256: payload.productContractSha256,
    withheldOracleSha256: payload.withheldOracleSha256,
    inputBundleSha256: payload.inputBundleSha256,
    artifactOnly: true,
    treatmentDisclosed: false,
    transcriptIncluded: false,
    diff: { path: payload.diffPath, sha256: payload.diffSha256 },
    verification: {
      receiptPath: payload.verificationReceiptPath,
      receiptSha256: payload.productDoneReceiptSha256,
      stdoutPath: payload.verificationStdoutPath,
      stdoutSha256: payload.verificationStdoutSha256,
      stderrPath: payload.verificationStderrPath,
      stderrSha256: payload.verificationStderrSha256,
    },
    changedPaths: payload.changedPaths,
    createdAt: payload.createdAt,
  };
  const bytes = `${JSON.stringify(packet, null, 2)}\n`;
  if (fs.existsSync(packetPath) && fs.readFileSync(packetPath, "utf8") !== bytes) {
    throw new Error(`immutable judge packet already differs: ${packetPath}`);
  }
  if (!fs.existsSync(packetPath)) writeJsonAtomic(packetPath, packet);
  return { path: packetPath, sha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(packetPath, "utf8")), packet };
}

function finalizePilotAttempt(manifest, opts, checkpoint) {
  const existing = readPilotResultRow(opts.pilotResults, checkpoint.attemptRunId);
  if (existing) {
    reconcileFinalizedCheckpoint(checkpoint, existing);
    console.log(`ALREADY_FINALIZED ${checkpoint.attemptRunId}: ${existing.result}`);
    return;
  }
  if (checkpoint.status === "finalized") throw new Error(`${checkpoint.attemptRunId} is finalized but its immutable result row is missing`);
  const actorRequest = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(checkpoint.requestPath, "utf8"));
  checkpoint = ensureActorRequest(checkpoint, {
    label: "actor",
    requestPath: checkpoint.requestPath,
    receiptPath: checkpoint.receiptPath,
    startPath: checkpoint.actorStartPath,
    requestSha256: checkpoint.requestSha256,
    launchNonce: checkpoint.actorLaunchNonce,
    timeoutMs: actorRequest.timeoutMs,
    status: "running",
    pidField: "actorPid",
  });
  const attempt = findPilotAttempt(manifest, checkpoint.attemptId);
  const resolved = require("./lib/acef-execution-assurance-experiment").resolveCatalogTask(manifest, opts.manifest, attempt.taskId);
  const verificationContract = resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.integration : resolved.task;
  const receipt = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(checkpoint.receiptPath, "utf8"));
  validateCheckpointInputs(opts, checkpoint, resolved, receipt, manifest);
  const claim = acquireFinalizationClaim(
    opts.pilotResults,
    checkpoint.attemptRunId,
    path.join(opts.pilotWorkspace, "finalization-locks"),
  );
  try {
    const racedResult = readPilotResultRow(opts.pilotResults, checkpoint.attemptRunId);
    if (racedResult) {
      reconcileFinalizedCheckpoint(checkpoint, racedResult);
      console.log(`ALREADY_FINALIZED ${checkpoint.attemptRunId}: ${racedResult.result}`);
      return;
    }
  const stdout = fs.readFileSync(checkpoint.rawPath, "utf8");
  const stderr = fs.readFileSync(`${checkpoint.rawPath}.stderr`, "utf8");
  const actor = {
    status: receipt.status,
    signal: receipt.signal,
    stdout,
    stderr,
    ...codexMetrics(parseJsonLines(checkpoint.rawPath)),
  };
  const activeDeliverySeconds = Math.round((new Date(receipt.finishedAt) - new Date(receipt.startedAt)) / 100) / 10;
  const verified = ensureVerification(checkpoint, verificationContract);
  checkpoint = verified.checkpoint;
  const verificationRequest = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(checkpoint.verificationRequestPath, "utf8"));
  const verification = {
    ...verified.verification,
    stdoutSha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(verificationRequest.stdoutPath, "utf8")),
    stderrSha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(verificationRequest.stderrPath, "utf8")),
  };
  const productDoneReceipt = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(checkpoint.verificationReceiptPath, "utf8"));
  const paths = changedPaths(checkpoint.clone, checkpoint.scoredBase);
  const allowedPaths = resolved.kind === "epic"
    ? [...new Set(resolved.task.stories.flatMap((story) => [...(story.allowedPaths || []), ...(story.testPaths || [])]))]
    : [...(resolved.task.allowedPaths || []), ...(resolved.task.testPaths || [])];
  const scopeViolations = paths.filter((entry) => !isPilotHarnessPath(entry) && !isAllowedPath(entry, allowedPaths));
  const expectationFailures = evaluateExpectations(checkpoint.clone, verificationContract.expected || [], resolved.fixtureRoot);
  const fullDiff = captureGitDiff(checkpoint.clone, checkpoint.scoredBase);
  const diff = captureGitDiff(checkpoint.clone, checkpoint.scoredBase, allowedPaths);
  const diffPath = path.join(opts.pilotWorkspace, "artifacts", `${checkpoint.attemptRunId}.patch`);
  const fullDiffPath = path.join(opts.pilotWorkspace, "artifacts", `${checkpoint.attemptRunId}.full.patch`);
  fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(diffPath), { recursive: true });
  fs.writeFileSync(diffPath, diff);
  fs.writeFileSync(fullDiffPath, fullDiff);
  const attemptFinishedAt = new Date().toISOString();
  const productDoneReceiptSha256 = sha256(fs.readFileSync(checkpoint.verificationReceiptPath, "utf8"));
  const productContract = frozenProductContract(resolved);
  const oracleSha256 = withheldOracleSha256(resolved);
  const inputBundleSha256 = sha256(JSON.stringify({
    productContractSha256: productContract.sha256,
    withheldOracleSha256: oracleSha256,
    productDiffSha256: sha256(diff),
    productChangedPaths: paths.filter((entry) => allowedPaths.some((allowed) => isAllowedPath(entry, [allowed]))),
    verificationReceiptSha256: productDoneReceiptSha256,
    verificationStdoutSha256: verification.stdoutSha256,
    verificationStderrSha256: verification.stderrSha256,
  }));
  const judgePacket = writeArtifactOnlyJudgePacket(opts, {
    experimentId: manifest.experimentId,
    attemptId: attempt.id,
    attemptRunId: checkpoint.attemptRunId,
    attemptOrdinal: checkpoint.attemptOrdinal,
    taskId: attempt.taskId,
    storyInventory: resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.stories.map((story) => story.id) : [resolved.taskId],
    project: resolved.repo,
    projectCommit: resolved.commit,
    productContract: productContract.contract,
    productContractSha256: productContract.sha256,
    withheldOracleSha256: oracleSha256,
    inputBundleSha256,
    diffPath,
    diffSha256: sha256(diff),
    verificationReceiptPath: checkpoint.verificationReceiptPath,
    productDoneReceiptSha256,
    verificationStdoutPath: verificationRequest.stdoutPath,
    verificationStdoutSha256: verification.stdoutSha256,
    verificationStderrPath: verificationRequest.stderrPath,
    verificationStderrSha256: verification.stderrSha256,
    changedPaths: paths.filter((entry) => isAllowedPath(entry, allowedPaths)),
    createdAt: attemptFinishedAt,
  });
  const traceOptions = {
    scopeIds: resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.stories.map((story) => story.id) : [resolved.taskId],
    retryableControls: attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3"
      ? ["codeReview", "patchAssurance"] : ["codeReview", "verifyPatch"],
    requiredControlsPerScope: attempt.treatment === "repo-native" ? []
      : attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3"
        ? ["readiness", "atdd", "development", "codeReview", "patchAssurance"]
        : ["readiness", "atdd", "development", "codeReview", "testReview", "processJudge"],
  };
  const lifecycleCommandTrace = parseIndependentTrace(actor.stdout, traceOptions);
  const harnessOracleTrace = parseIndependentTrace(`scope=epic ${verificationContract.verify.join(" ")}\n`, {
    scopeIds: traceOptions.scopeIds, requiredControlsPerScope: [],
  });
  const commandTrace = parseIndependentTrace(`${actor.stdout}\nscope=epic ${verificationContract.verify.join(" ")}\n`, traceOptions);
  const actorContract = resolved.kind === "epic" && attempt.treatment !== "repo-native"
    ? lifecycleActorContract(resolved, attempt.actorContractVersion) : [];
  const treatmentState = evaluateTreatmentState(checkpoint.clone, attempt,
    resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.stories.map((story) => story.id) : [resolved.taskId],
    checkpoint.attemptRunId);
  const discoveryContracts = validateFrozenDiscoveryContracts(checkpoint.clone, resolved, attempt);
  const collaborationEvidence = actorContract.length
    ? loadCollaborationEvidence(checkpoint.rawPath, actorContract, {
      cwd: checkpoint.clone,
      clientVersion: checkpoint.observedClientVersion.replace(/^codex-cli\s+/, ""),
      startedAt: receipt.startedAt,
      finishedAt: receipt.finishedAt,
      allowUnexpectedActors: attempt.treatment === "legacy",
      legacyPolicy: attempt.treatment === "legacy",
      actorContractVersion: attempt.actorContractVersion,
      actorRuntimeProfiles: manifest.actorRuntimeProfiles || null,
      runtimeContract: attempt.runtimeContract || null,
      maximumActorInvocations: manifest.promotionGates?.budget?.maximumActorInvocations,
      lifecycleIntegrationArgv: attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3"
        ? verificationContract.verify : null,
    })
    : { ok: true, expectedActorCount: 0, observedActorCount: 0, dispatches: [], failures: [] };
  const childMetrics = collaborationEvidence.childMetrics
    || { input_tokens: 0, cached_input_tokens: 0, output_tokens: 0, model_cycles: 0, tool_calls: 0, commandText: "" };
  const teamMetrics = aggregateTeamMetrics(actor, childMetrics);
  const teamLifecycleCommandTrace = parseIndependentTrace(
    `${actor.stdout}\n${childMetrics.commandText || ""}`,
    traceOptions,
  );
  const durableLifecycleEvidence = actorContract.length
    ? validateDurableLifecycleEvidence(
      checkpoint.clone,
      collaborationEvidence.actorContract || actorContract,
      collaborationEvidence.acceptedActors || actorContract,
      {
        actorContractVersion: attempt.actorContractVersion,
        runId: treatmentState.observed?.runId,
        storyInventory: resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.stories.map((story) => story.id) : [resolved.taskId],
        stories: resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.stories : [resolved.task],
        developerReactivations: collaborationEvidence.developerReactivations || [],
        reviewerCompletions: collaborationEvidence.reviewerCompletions || [],
        lifecycleIntegration: collaborationEvidence.lifecycleIntegration || null,
      },
    )
    : { ok: true, actorCount: 0, gateCount: 0, failures: [] };
  const trace = actorContract.length
    ? parseLifecycleDispatchTrace(collaborationEvidence.dispatchTraceContract || collaborationEvidence.actorContract || [], {
      scopeIds: resolved.task.stories.map((story) => story.id),
      maximumRetryOrdinal: attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3" ? 2 : 1,
      globalRepairCycles: attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3",
      requiredControlsPerScope: attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3"
        ? ["atdd", "development", "code-review", "patch-assurance"]
        : ["atdd", "development", "code-review", "verify-patch", "test-review", "process-judge"],
    })
    : commandTrace;
  if (actorContract.length) {
    checkpoint = {
      ...checkpoint,
      collaborationThreadId: collaborationEvidence.threadId || null,
      collaborationSessionPath: collaborationEvidence.sessionPath || null,
      collaborationSessionSha256: collaborationEvidence.sessionSha256 || null,
    };
    writeJsonAtomic(checkpoint.checkpointPath, checkpoint);
  }
  const harnessWait = collaborationEvidence.sessionPath && fs.existsSync(collaborationEvidence.sessionPath)
    ? parseHarnessWaitMetrics(fs.readFileSync(collaborationEvidence.sessionPath, "utf8"), activeDeliverySeconds, collaborationEvidence)
    : parseHarnessWaitMetrics("", activeDeliverySeconds, collaborationEvidence);
  const pilotBudgets = evaluatePilotBudgets(
    manifest, attempt, activeDeliverySeconds, teamMetrics, collaborationEvidence,
    attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3" ? teamLifecycleCommandTrace : commandTrace,
    harnessWait,
  );
  const processOraclePassed = actor.status === 0 && verification.status === 0
    && scopeViolations.length === 0 && expectationFailures.length === 0
    && collaborationEvidence.ok && durableLifecycleEvidence.ok
    && (!actorContract.length || collaborationEvidence.closeoutCreatedMandatoryChains === 0)
    && trace.scopeAttributionComplete && trace.lifecycleComplete && !trace.duplicateLifecycle
    && treatmentState.ok && discoveryContracts.ok;
  const automatedOraclePassed = processOraclePassed && pilotBudgets.ok;
  const row = {
    schema: "acef.execution-assurance-pilot-attempt.v1",
    experimentId: manifest.experimentId,
    attemptId: attempt.id,
    attemptOrdinal: checkpoint.attemptOrdinal,
    attemptRunId: checkpoint.attemptRunId,
    order: attempt.order,
    taskId: attempt.taskId,
    storyInventory: resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.stories.map((story) => story.id) : [resolved.taskId],
    treatment: attempt.treatment,
    workflowId: attempt.workflowId,
    assuranceProfile: attempt.assuranceProfile,
    actorContractVersion: attempt.actorContractVersion,
    frameworkCommit: attempt.frameworkCommit,
    project: resolved.repo,
    projectCommit: resolved.commit,
    client: manifest.pilotRuntime.client,
    clientPath: checkpoint.clientPath,
    clientBinarySha256: checkpoint.clientBinarySha256,
    clientVersion: checkpoint.observedClientVersion,
    model: manifest.pilotRuntime.model,
    reasoningEffort: manifest.pilotRuntime.reasoningEffort,
    startedAt: receipt.startedAt,
    finishedAt: attemptFinishedAt,
    activeDeliverySeconds,
    wallTimeToProductDoneSeconds: null,
    timeToFirstValidGreenSeconds: null,
    frameworkRuntimeSeconds: attempt.treatment === "repo-native" ? 0 : null,
    capped: actor.signal !== null,
    activeTimeCapMinutes: attempt.activeTimeCapMinutes,
    actorExitCode: actor.status,
    verificationExitCode: verification.status,
    verificationCommandSha256: checkpoint.verificationCommandSha256,
    verificationReceiptPath: checkpoint.verificationReceiptPath,
    verificationStdoutSha256: verification.stdoutSha256,
    verificationStderrSha256: verification.stderrSha256,
    productDoneReceiptPath: checkpoint.verificationReceiptPath,
    productDoneReceiptSha256,
    harnessProductDoneAt: verification.status === 0 ? productDoneReceipt.finishedAt : null,
    judgePacketPath: judgePacket.path,
    judgePacketSha256: judgePacket.sha256,
    judgeLaunchRoot: path.join(opts.pilotWorkspace, "blind-judge", checkpoint.attemptRunId),
    inputTokens: teamMetrics.input_tokens,
    cachedInputTokens: teamMetrics.cached_input_tokens,
    outputTokens: teamMetrics.output_tokens,
    modelCycles: teamMetrics.model_cycles,
    toolCalls: teamMetrics.tool_calls,
    conductorMetrics: {
      inputTokens: actor.input_tokens,
      cachedInputTokens: actor.cached_input_tokens,
      outputTokens: actor.output_tokens,
      modelCycles: actor.model_cycles,
      toolCalls: actor.tool_calls,
    },
    teamMetrics,
    changedPaths: paths,
    scopeViolations,
    expectationFailures,
    independentTrace: trace,
    commandTrace,
    lifecycleCommandTrace: attempt.actorContractVersion === "four-actor-v3" ? teamLifecycleCommandTrace : lifecycleCommandTrace,
    harnessOracleTrace,
    collaborationEvidence,
    durableLifecycleEvidence,
    treatmentState,
    discoveryContracts,
    processOraclePassed,
    harnessWait,
    pilotBudgets,
    transcriptPath: checkpoint.rawPath,
    transcriptSha256: sha256(actor.stdout),
    stderrSha256: sha256(actor.stderr),
    diffPath,
    diffSha256: sha256(diff),
    fullDiffPath,
    fullDiffSha256: sha256(fullDiff),
    productContractSha256: productContract.sha256,
    withheldOracleSha256: oracleSha256,
    judgeInputBundleSha256: inputBundleSha256,
    automatedOraclePassed,
    blindJudgeStatus: "pending",
    productDone: false,
    result: automatedOraclePassed ? "PROVISIONAL_PASS" : "FAIL",
  };
  fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(opts.pilotResults), { recursive: true });
  fs.appendFileSync(opts.pilotResults, `${JSON.stringify(row)}\n`);
  writeJsonAtomic(checkpoint.checkpointPath, { ...checkpoint, status: "finalized", finalizedAt: row.finishedAt, result: row.result });
  console.log(`${row.result} ${attempt.id}: automated=${automatedOraclePassed ? "PASS" : "FAIL"}; blind-judge=pending; product-done=false; active=${activeDeliverySeconds}s`);
  console.log(`ARTIFACT ${diffPath}`);
  } finally {
    claim.release();
  }
}

function readJsonlRows(filePath) {
  if (!fs.existsSync(filePath)) return [];
  return fs.readFileSync(filePath, "utf8").split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean).map((line, index) => {
    try { return JSON.parse(line); }
    catch { throw new Error(`${filePath}:${index + 1} is invalid JSON`); }
  });
}

function blindJudgePrompt(packet) {
  return [
    "You are the independent blind product Judge for one controlled experiment attempt.",
    "Use only the immutable artifact-only packet and the product/test artifacts it names. Do not inspect process-control state or docs, implementation transcripts, workflow labels, or other runs.",
    `Packet path: ${packet._packetPath}`,
    `Frozen product contract SHA256: ${packet.productContractSha256}`,
    `Judge input bundle SHA256: ${packet.inputBundleSha256}`,
    "Judge whether the product contract is complete and correct. Return one final answer with these exact lines:",
    `JUDGE_PACKET_SHA256=${packet._packetSha256}`,
    `JUDGE_INPUT_BUNDLE_SHA256=${packet.inputBundleSha256}`,
    `PRODUCT_CONTRACT_SHA256=${packet.productContractSha256}`,
    "JUDGE_VERDICT=<PASS|FAIL|PENDING>",
    "PRODUCT_OUTCOME_COMPLETE=<true|false>",
    "SCOPE_VIOLATION=<true|false>",
    "TEST_WEAKENING=<true|false>",
    "FINDINGS_SHA256=<sha256 of canonical JSON findings array>",
    "JUDGMENT_JSON_BASE64=<canonical base64 of a JSON object with verdict, productOutcomeComplete, scopeViolation, testWeakening, and findings>",
    "Each finding must have a unique id and severity CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW. PASS requires an empty unresolved Critical/High set.",
  ].join("\n");
}

function judgeFinalAnswerFromTranscript(sessionText) {
  const answers = String(sessionText || "").split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean).flatMap((line) => {
    let row;
    try { row = JSON.parse(line); } catch { return []; }
    const payload = row.payload || {};
    if (row.type === "event_msg" && payload.type === "agent_message" && payload.phase === "final_answer") {
      return [String(payload.message || "")];
    }
    if (row.type === "response_item" && payload.type === "agent_message") {
      return [Array.isArray(payload.content) ? payload.content.map((entry) => entry.text || entry.output_text || "").join("\n") : String(payload.text || "")];
    }
    return [];
  }).filter((text) => /JUDGMENT_JSON_BASE64=/.test(text));
  if (!answers.length) throw new Error("pinned blind Judge did not return a machine-bound final answer");
  return answers.at(-1);
}

function runPilotJudge(manifest, opts) {
  const attempt = readPilotResultRow(opts.pilotResults, opts.pilotJudge);
  if (!attempt) throw new Error(`immutable pilot attempt not found: ${opts.pilotJudge}`);
  if (!fs.existsSync(attempt.judgePacketPath)
    || sha256(fs.readFileSync(attempt.judgePacketPath, "utf8")) !== attempt.judgePacketSha256) {
    throw new Error("immutable Judge packet is missing or changed");
  }
  const packet = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(attempt.judgePacketPath, "utf8"));
  packet._packetPath = attempt.judgePacketPath;
  packet._packetSha256 = attempt.judgePacketSha256;
  const runtime = resolvePinnedClient(manifest.pilotRuntime);
  const priorJudgments = readJsonlRows(opts.pilotJudgments).filter((entry) => entry.attemptRunId === attempt.attemptRunId);
  if (priorJudgments.some((entry) => entry.verdict !== "PENDING")) {
    throw new Error(`${attempt.attemptRunId} already has a terminal blind judgment`);
  }
  const ordinal = priorJudgments.length + 1;
  const launchRoot = path.join(attempt.judgeLaunchRoot, `judge-${ordinal}`);
  fs.mkdirSync(launchRoot, { recursive: true });
  const prompt = blindJudgePrompt(packet);
  const rawPath = path.join(launchRoot, "session-output.jsonl");
  const actorReceiptPath = path.join(launchRoot, "actor-receipt.json");
  const requestPath = path.join(launchRoot, "request.json");
  const checkpointPath = path.join(launchRoot, "checkpoint.json");
  const request = {
    command: runtime.clientPath,
    args: [
      "exec", "--json", "--ignore-user-config", "--ignore-rules",
      "--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox", "--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust",
      "--model", manifest.pilotRuntime.model,
      "--config", `model_reasoning_effort=${JSON.stringify(manifest.pilotRuntime.reasoningEffort)}`,
      "-C", launchRoot, prompt,
    ],
    cwd: launchRoot,
    stdoutPath: rawPath,
    stderrPath: `${rawPath}.stderr`,
    receiptPath: actorReceiptPath,
    startPath: `${rawPath}.started.json`,
    launchNonce: `${attempt.attemptRunId}:blind-judge:${ordinal}:v1`,
    timeoutMs: 1800000,
  };
  writeJsonAtomic(requestPath, request);
  const checkpoint = {
    schema: "acef.execution-assurance-judge-checkpoint.v1", experimentId: manifest.experimentId,
    attemptRunId: attempt.attemptRunId, checkpointPath, clone: launchRoot, status: "prepared",
  };
  writeJsonAtomic(checkpointPath, checkpoint);
  ensureActorRequest(checkpoint, {
    label: "blind-judge", requestPath, receiptPath: actorReceiptPath, startPath: request.startPath,
    requestSha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(requestPath, "utf8")), launchNonce: request.launchNonce,
    timeoutMs: request.timeoutMs, status: "judging", pidField: "judgePid",
  });
  const actorReceipt = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(actorReceiptPath, "utf8"));
  if (actorReceipt.status !== 0) throw new Error(`pinned blind Judge exited ${actorReceipt.status}`);
  let threadId = null;
  for (const line of fs.readFileSync(rawPath, "utf8").split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean)) {
    try { const row = JSON.parse(line); if (row.type === "thread.started") threadId = row.thread_id; } catch {}
  }
  const sessionTranscriptPath = findCodexSessionTranscript(threadId);
  if (!sessionTranscriptPath) throw new Error("pinned blind Judge session transcript is missing");
  const sessionText = fs.readFileSync(sessionTranscriptPath, "utf8");
  const finalAnswer = judgeFinalAnswerFromTranscript(sessionText);
  const base64 = finalAnswer.match(/^JUDGMENT_JSON_BASE64=([A-Za-z0-9+/=]+)$/m)?.[1] || "";
  const judgmentPayloadBytes = Buffer.from(base64, "base64");
  if (!base64 || judgmentPayloadBytes.toString("base64") !== base64) throw new Error("blind Judge judgment payload is not canonical base64");
  const payload = JSON.parse(judgmentPayloadBytes.toString("utf8"));
  const meta = sessionText.split(/\r?\n/).filter(Boolean).flatMap((line) => {
    try { const row = JSON.parse(line); return row.type === "session_meta" ? [row.payload || {}] : []; } catch { return []; }
  })[0];
  const judgeSessionId = meta?.id || meta?.session_id || "";
  const judgeReceiptPath = path.join(launchRoot, "judge-receipt.json");
  const judgeReceipt = {
    schema: "acef.execution-assurance-judge-receipt.v1", experimentId: manifest.experimentId,
    attemptRunId: attempt.attemptRunId, judgePacketSha256: attempt.judgePacketSha256,
    inputBundleSha256: attempt.judgeInputBundleSha256, productContractSha256: attempt.productContractSha256,
    judgeSessionId, sessionTranscriptPath, sessionTranscriptSha256: sha256(sessionText),
    freshSession: true, artifactOnly: true, treatmentBlinded: true, transcriptWithheld: true,
    crossRunMemory: false, parentSessionId: null, judgeModel: manifest.pilotRuntime.model,
    reasoningEffort: manifest.pilotRuntime.reasoningEffort, clientPath: runtime.clientPath,
    clientBinarySha256: runtime.clientBinarySha256, clientVersion: runtime.observedClientVersion,
    requestPath, requestSha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(requestPath, "utf8")),
    actorReceiptPath, actorReceiptSha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(actorReceiptPath, "utf8")),
    promptSha256: sha256(prompt), startedAt: actorReceipt.startedAt, finishedAt: actorReceipt.finishedAt,
  };
  writeJsonAtomic(judgeReceiptPath, judgeReceipt);
  const judgment = {
    schema: "acef.execution-assurance-pilot-judgment.v3", experimentId: manifest.experimentId,
    attemptId: attempt.attemptId, attemptRunId: attempt.attemptRunId, attemptOrdinal: attempt.attemptOrdinal,
    diffSha256: attempt.diffSha256, judgePacketId: `J-${ordinal}-${sha256(sessionText).slice(0, 12)}`,
    judgePacketSha256: attempt.judgePacketSha256, judgeModel: manifest.pilotRuntime.model,
    judgeReceiptPath, judgeReceiptSha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(judgeReceiptPath, "utf8")), judgeSessionId,
    productDoneReceiptSha256: attempt.productDoneReceiptSha256, treatmentBlinded: true, transcriptWithheld: true,
    scopeViolation: payload.scopeViolation, testWeakening: payload.testWeakening,
    verdict: payload.verdict, findings: payload.findings, productOutcomeComplete: payload.productOutcomeComplete,
    judgedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
  };
  const judgmentPath = path.join(launchRoot, "judgment.json");
  writeJsonAtomic(judgmentPath, judgment);
  return ingestPilotJudgment(manifest, { ...opts, pilotIngestJudgment: judgmentPath });
}

function ingestPilotJudgment(manifest, opts) {
  if (!fs.existsSync(opts.pilotIngestJudgment) || !fs.statSync(opts.pilotIngestJudgment).isFile()) {
    throw new Error("judgment input must be an existing JSON file");
  }
  const judgment = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(opts.pilotIngestJudgment, "utf8"));
  const attempt = readPilotResultRow(opts.pilotResults, judgment.attemptRunId);
  if (!attempt) throw new Error(`immutable pilot attempt not found: ${judgment.attemptRunId || "missing attemptRunId"}`);
  const verdict = derivePilotVerdict(manifest, attempt, judgment);
  const safeRun = String(judgment.attemptRunId).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9._-]/g, "_");
  const safePacket = String(judgment.judgePacketId).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9._-]/g, "_");
  const verdictPath = path.join(opts.pilotVerdictDirectory, `${safeRun}--${safePacket}.json`);
  const claim = acquireFinalizationClaim(
    opts.pilotJudgments,
    `judgment-${safeRun}-${safePacket}`,
    path.join(opts.pilotWorkspace, "judgment-locks"),
  );
  try {
    const judgments = readJsonlRows(opts.pilotJudgments);
    const existingJudgment = judgments.find((entry) => entry.judgePacketId === judgment.judgePacketId);
    if (existingJudgment && sha256(JSON.stringify(existingJudgment)) !== sha256(JSON.stringify(judgment))) {
      throw new Error(`judgePacketId ${judgment.judgePacketId} already exists with different immutable content`);
    }
    const terminalJudgment = judgments.find((entry) => entry.experimentId === judgment.experimentId
      && entry.attemptRunId === judgment.attemptRunId && entry.verdict !== "PENDING");
    if (!existingJudgment && terminalJudgment) {
      throw new Error(`attempt ${judgment.attemptRunId} already has terminal ${terminalJudgment.verdict} judgment; only PENDING is supersedable`);
    }
    const reusedJudgeSession = judgments.find((entry) => entry.experimentId === judgment.experimentId
      && entry.attemptRunId === judgment.attemptRunId && entry.judgeSessionId === judgment.judgeSessionId
      && entry.judgePacketId !== judgment.judgePacketId);
    if (!existingJudgment && reusedJudgeSession) {
      throw new Error(`judge session ${judgment.judgeSessionId} is not fresh for packet ${judgment.judgePacketId}`);
    }
    if (fs.existsSync(verdictPath)) {
      const existingVerdict = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(verdictPath, "utf8"));
      if (sha256(JSON.stringify(existingVerdict)) !== sha256(JSON.stringify(verdict))) {
        throw new Error(`immutable verdict artifact already differs: ${verdictPath}`);
      }
    } else {
      writeJsonAtomic(verdictPath, verdict);
    }
    if (!existingJudgment) {
      fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(opts.pilotJudgments), { recursive: true });
      fs.appendFileSync(opts.pilotJudgments, `${JSON.stringify(judgment)}\n`);
    }
    console.log(`${existingJudgment ? "ALREADY_INGESTED" : "INGESTED"} ${judgment.judgePacketId}: ${verdict.result}`);
    console.log(`VERDICT ${verdictPath}`);
    return { judgment, verdict, verdictPath, alreadyIngested: Boolean(existingJudgment) };
  } finally {
    claim.release();
  }
}

function runPilotAttempt(manifest, opts) {
  const attempt = findPilotAttempt(manifest, opts.pilotRun);
  const history = pilotAttemptHistory(opts.pilotResults, attempt.id);
  if (history.maxOrdinal > 0) {
    if (!history.latest?.invalidated) {
      throw new Error(`pilot attempt ${attempt.id} already has an immutable result row`);
    }
    if (!opts.pilotRetryInvalidated) {
      throw new Error(`pilot attempt ${attempt.id} was invalidated; rerun requires --pilot-retry-invalidated`);
    }
  }
  if (must("git", ["status", "--porcelain"], root) !== "") {
    throw new Error(`${attempt.id}: runner worktree must be clean before a scored pilot launch`);
  }
  const clientRuntime = resolvePinnedClient(manifest.pilotRuntime);
  const resolved = resolveCatalogTask(manifest, opts.manifest, attempt.taskId);
  if (!fs.existsSync(opts.preflightOutput)) throw new Error(`${attempt.id}: pilot preflight artifact is missing`);
  const pilotPreflight = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(opts.preflightOutput, "utf8"));
  const preflightFailures = [];
  if (!pilotPreflight.ok) preflightFailures.push("pilot preflight is not PASS");
  if (!pilotPreflight.collaborationCanary?.ok) preflightFailures.push("collaboration canary is not PASS");
  if (pilotPreflight.runnerDirtyBefore !== false) preflightFailures.push("preflight runner worktree was dirty");
  if (pilotPreflight.runnerSourceSha256 !== runnerSourceSha256()) preflightFailures.push("preflight runner source drift");
  if (pilotPreflight.manifestSha256 !== sha256(fs.readFileSync(opts.manifest, "utf8"))) preflightFailures.push("preflight manifest binding drift");
  const preflightTaskBinding = (pilotPreflight.taskBindings || []).find((entry) => entry.taskId === attempt.taskId);
  if (!preflightTaskBinding || preflightTaskBinding.resolvedTaskSha256 !== resolvedTaskSha256(resolved)) {
    preflightFailures.push("preflight resolved task/fixture binding drift");
  }
  const preflightEnvironmentProbe = (pilotPreflight.environmentProbes || []).find((entry) => entry.taskId === attempt.taskId);
  if (!preflightEnvironmentProbe?.ok) preflightFailures.push("preflight real environment probe is not PASS");
  if (pilotPreflight.collaborationCanary?.clientBinarySha256 !== clientRuntime.clientBinarySha256) preflightFailures.push("preflight client binary drift");
  if (pilotPreflight.collaborationCanary?.clientVersion !== clientRuntime.observedClientVersion) preflightFailures.push("preflight client version drift");
  if (preflightFailures.length) throw new Error(`${attempt.id}: ${preflightFailures.join("; ")}`);
  const attemptOrdinal = history.maxOrdinal + 1;
  if (resolved.kind === "story") {
    throw new Error(`${attempt.id} story treatment execution is not enabled until exact-version compact lifecycle orchestration is wired`);
  }
  if (resolved.kind === "task" && attempt.treatment !== "repo-native") {
    throw new Error(`${attempt.id} ACEF single-task execution is not enabled until exact-version compact lifecycle orchestration is wired`);
  }
  const executionAttempt = { ...attempt, id: attemptOrdinal === 1 ? attempt.id : `${attempt.id}-r${attemptOrdinal}` };
  const checkpointPath = pilotCheckpointPath(opts, executionAttempt.id);
  if (fs.existsSync(checkpointPath)) {
    throw new Error(`${executionAttempt.id} already has a durable checkpoint; use --pilot-finalize ${attempt.id}`);
  }
  const prepared = resolved.kind === "epic"
    ? prepareEpicClone(resolved, executionAttempt, opts)
    : prepareSingleTaskClone(resolved, executionAttempt, opts);
  installExactFramework(prepared.clone, attempt, manifest, opts);
  const launchEnvironmentProbe = runTaskEnvironmentProbe(resolved, opts, `${executionAttempt.id}-launch`, prepared.clone);
  if (!launchEnvironmentProbe.ok) throw new Error(`${attempt.id}: launch environment probe failed before timed execution`);
  const verificationContract = resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.integration : resolved.task;
  const preconditions = resolved.kind === "epic" ? resolved.task.stories : [resolved.task];
  for (const contract of preconditions) {
    const precondition = execute(contract.verify[0], contract.verify.slice(1), prepared.clone, { timeout: 600000 });
    if (precondition.status === 0) throw new Error(`${attempt.id}: ${contract.id || resolved.taskId} seeded precondition is not red`);
    if (!isBehavioralRed(precondition)) {
      throw new Error(`${attempt.id}: ${contract.id || resolved.taskId} precondition failed for a non-behavioral reason`);
    }
  }
  const scoredBase = commitAll(prepared.clone, `chore: freeze ${attempt.id} scored base`);
  const rawPath = path.join(opts.pilotWorkspace, "raw", `${executionAttempt.id}.jsonl`);
  const receiptPath = path.join(opts.pilotWorkspace, "receipts", `${executionAttempt.id}.json`);
  const requestPath = path.join(opts.pilotWorkspace, "requests", `${executionAttempt.id}.json`);
  const request = pilotAgentRequest(executionAttempt, resolved, prepared.clone, manifest, rawPath, receiptPath, clientRuntime);
  request.startPath = `${rawPath}.started.json`;
  request.launchNonce = `${executionAttempt.id}:actor:v1`;
  writeJsonAtomic(requestPath, request);
  const checkpoint = {
    schema: "acef.execution-assurance-pilot-checkpoint.v1",
    experimentId: manifest.experimentId,
    checkpointPath,
    attemptId: attempt.id,
    attemptOrdinal,
    attemptRunId: executionAttempt.id,
    clone: prepared.clone,
    scoredBase,
    rawPath,
    requestPath,
    receiptPath,
    actorStartPath: request.startPath,
    actorLaunchNonce: request.launchNonce,
    requestSha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(requestPath, "utf8")),
    manifestPath: path.resolve(opts.manifest),
    manifestSha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(opts.manifest, "utf8")),
    resolvedTaskSha256: resolvedTaskSha256(resolved),
    pilotResultsPath: path.resolve(opts.pilotResults),
    runnerCommit: must("git", ["rev-parse", "HEAD"], root),
    runnerWorktreeSha256: sha256(must("git", ["status", "--porcelain"], root)),
    clientPath: clientRuntime.clientPath,
    clientBinarySha256: clientRuntime.clientBinarySha256,
    observedClientVersion: clientRuntime.observedClientVersion,
    status: "prepared",
    preparedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
  };
  writeJsonAtomic(checkpointPath, checkpoint);
  const runningCheckpoint = ensureActorRequest(checkpoint, {
    label: "actor",
    requestPath,
    receiptPath,
    startPath: request.startPath,
    requestSha256: checkpoint.requestSha256,
    launchNonce: request.launchNonce,
    timeoutMs: request.timeoutMs,
    status: "running",
    pidField: "actorPid",
  });
  finalizePilotAttempt(manifest, opts, runningCheckpoint);
}

function main() {
  const opts = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));
  const manifest = validateManifest(JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(opts.manifest, "utf8")));
  if (opts.plan) {
    console.log(JSON.stringify({
      experimentId: manifest.experimentId,
      treatments: manifest.treatments,
      count: manifest.pilot.attempts.length,
      attempts: buildPilotPlan(manifest),
    }, null, 2));
    return;
  }
  if (opts.pilotPreflight) {
    if (fs.existsSync(opts.preflightOutput) && !opts.force) {
      throw new Error(`immutable pilot preflight already exists at ${opts.preflightOutput}; use --force only for a documented rerun`);
    }
    const runnerDirtyBefore = must("git", ["status", "--porcelain"], root) !== "";
    const preflight = preflightCatalog(manifest, opts.manifest);
    const collaborationCanary = runCollaborationCanary(manifest);
    const environmentProbes = Object.keys(manifest.taskCatalog || {}).sort().map((taskId) => {
      try {
        return runTaskEnvironmentProbe(resolveCatalogTask(manifest, opts.manifest, taskId), opts, `preflight-${taskId}`);
      } catch (error) {
        return { taskId, ok: false, commands: [], error: error.message };
      }
    });
    const referenceValidations = Object.keys(manifest.taskCatalog || {}).sort().map((taskId) => {
      try {
        return runTaskReferenceValidation(resolveCatalogTask(manifest, opts.manifest, taskId), opts, `preflight-${taskId}`);
      } catch (error) {
        return { taskId, ok: false, required: true, stories: [], error: error.message };
      }
    });
    const row = {
      schema: "acef.execution-assurance-pilot-preflight.v1",
      experimentId: manifest.experimentId,
      candidateCommit: manifest.treatments.candidate.commit,
      manifestSha256: sha256(fs.readFileSync(opts.manifest, "utf8")),
      runnerCommit: must("git", ["rev-parse", "HEAD"], root),
      runnerDirtyBefore,
      runnerSourceSha256: runnerSourceSha256(),
      taskBindings: catalogTaskBindings(manifest, opts.manifest),
      checkedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
      ...preflight,
      collaborationCanary,
      environmentProbes,
      referenceValidations,
      ok: preflight.ok && collaborationCanary.ok && environmentProbes.every((entry) => entry.ok)
        && referenceValidations.every((entry) => entry.ok),
    };
    writeJson(opts.preflightOutput, row);
    for (const check of row.checks) console.log(`${check.ok ? "PASS" : "FAIL"} ${check.taskId}${check.blockers.length ? `: ${check.blockers.join("; ")}` : ""}`);
    console.log(`${collaborationCanary.ok ? "PASS" : "FAIL"} collaboration-canary${collaborationCanary.failures.length ? `: ${collaborationCanary.failures.join("; ")}` : ""}`);
    for (const probe of environmentProbes) console.log(`${probe.ok ? "PASS" : "FAIL"} environment-probe ${probe.taskId}${probe.error ? `: ${probe.error}` : ""}`);
    for (const validation of referenceValidations) console.log(`${validation.ok ? "PASS" : "FAIL"} reference-validation ${validation.taskId}${validation.error ? `: ${validation.error}` : ""}`);
    console.log(`PILOT_PREFLIGHT ${row.ok ? "PASS" : "FAIL"}: ${row.checks.filter((check) => check.ok).length}/${row.checks.length} tasks ready`);
    if (!row.ok) process.exitCode = 1;
    return;
  }
  if (opts.pilotRun) {
    if (manifest.pilotRunAllowed === false) throw new Error("pilot run is disabled for this non-scored preparation manifest");
    runPilotAttempt(manifest, opts);
    return;
  }
  if (opts.pilotFinalize) {
    finalizePilotAttempt(manifest, opts, latestPilotCheckpoint(opts, opts.pilotFinalize));
    return;
  }
  if (opts.pilotJudge) {
    runPilotJudge(manifest, opts);
    return;
  }
  if (opts.pilotIngestJudgment) {
    ingestPilotJudgment(manifest, opts);
    return;
  }
  runStage0(manifest, opts);
}

if (require.main === module) {
  try {
    main();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`ACEF_EXECUTION_ASSURANCE_EXPERIMENT_ERROR: ${error.message}`);
    process.exitCode = 1;
  }
}

